1
00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.096
[Phone rings]

2
00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:01.600
[Tommy] Hello?

3
00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:03.677
[Branch]‘Hey, guys. It’s John Branch from “The NY Times”.
嗨，哥们，我是《纽约时报》的John Branch

4
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.262
‘How’s it going up there?’
你们怎样？

5
00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:06.972
[Tommy] Good, John.
挺好，John

6
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:09.683
[Branch]‘How high up are you guys right now?’
哥们，你们现在位置多高？

7
00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.487
[Tommy] We are about 1,200 feet up the wall at our base camp.
我们在1200英尺高的黎明墙（Dawn Wall）基地大本营

8
00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:16.190
This has been our home for nine days now.
目前也是我们九天中的家

9
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.153
[Branch]‘Tommy, I guess the bottom line question here,
Tommy，我想问，最根本的是

10
00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:21.703
‘why are you doing this?
为何你们这么做？

11
00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.702
‘What’s the point of all this for you?’
对于你们这意味着什么？

12
00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:32.335
[Presenter 1] On the air tonight with a story of two men
今晚的故事是，空中的两位

13
00:01:32.551 --> 00:01:35.418
attempting to free climb the famously steep face
正在著名的加州优胜美地国家公园 （Yosemite ）陡峭的El Capitan 岩墙 (世界上最大单体花岗岩)


14
00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.003
of El Capitan in Yosemite.
进行徒手攀岩

15
00:01:42.269 --> 00:01:44.601
[Presenter 2]
Inch by nerve-racking inch,
一英寸接着恼人的一英寸

16
00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:48.931
using only their fingertips to grasp razor sharp edges.
用他们的指尖去抓握住刀片般的锋利岩石边缘

17
00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:51.312
[Presenter 3]Tommy Caidwell and Kevin Jorgeson
Tommy Caidwell和 Kevin Jorgeson

18
00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:53.689
attempt the hardest climb in the world.
在进行世上最艰难的攀岩

19
00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:57.068
[Presenter 4] No one has ever free-climbed the Dawn Wall.
从未有人徒手攀爬过黎明墙 （the Dawn Wall）

20
00:01:57.284 --> 00:02:00.151
[Presenter 5] 3,000 feet of straight-up granite.
它是3000英尺高、直上直下的单体花岗岩

21
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.831
[Presenter 6] A climb watched by the world.
这次攀岩,全球都在观看中

22
00:02:11.048 --> 00:02:14.586
[Presenter 7]  These guys have captured the world’s attention.
他们俩也吸引了全球关注

23
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:18.593
[Presenter 8] They’re trying to make history.
他们想要创造历史

24
00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.593
[Presenter 9] El Capitan’s infamous Dawn Wall.
El Capitan 名声在外的黎明墙

25
00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.902
[Mom]As a kid, Tommy was slow at everything.
Tommy 从小就样样迟缓

26
00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.621
He had a lot of difficulty in school.
他在学校也有挺多困难

27
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.449
The teachers actually at one point told us
老师有次告诉我们

28
00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.127
that he was mentally retarded and would never learn.
他可能智力迟缓，很难学会什么

29
00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:57.504
I was developmentally delayed through... probably still.
我一直都发展延迟 ......可能都静止了

30
00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:03.005
I was this very fragile little kid
打小就很脆弱


31
00:03:03.225 --> 00:03:04.931
incredibly shy.
还异常羞怯

32
00:03:05.143 --> 00:03:09.682
But meanwhile, my dad was, like, the symbol of a man.
与此同时，我老爸却是人中龙凤

33
00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:16.025
He was this big bodybuilder dude and mountain climber.
他是大大有名的健美明星和登山选手


34
00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.194
Larger than life.
生活的强者

35
00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:20.147
[Dad]Tommy was small.
Tommy 那时很小

36
00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.699
He was way behind.
远远落在别人后面

37
00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:25.118
Didn’t crawl until he was over two.
两岁多才学会爬着走

38
00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.740
[Tommy] I think my dad felt
我猜我老爹是这么想的：

39
00:03:26.957 --> 00:03:29.118
the best way to prepare this fragile little kid for the world
培养这个脆弱小仔的最好方法是

40
00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.666
was to toughen him up a little bit.
要对他严厉一点

41
00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:36.037
So he took me on all these adventures.
所以他带着我去参加所有的冒险运动

42
00:03:36.258 --> 00:03:38.089
[Dad]Three years old, strap on the skis.
三岁时，被困在滑雪中

43
00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:40.838
[Tommy] Camping in a snow cave during a blizzard.
暴风雪期间，也到雪窟里去露营

44
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:44.091
Every summer, we’d go to Yosemite with my family,
每年夏天，全家一起去优胜美地

45
00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:47.299
and my dad would take me climbing on these giant walls.
我老爹就带我去爬那些巨大的岩墙

46
00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:51.387
Some of the craziest climbing stunts you could ever do
有些最惊人的攀岩特技，别人不敢做的

47
00:03:51.606 --> 00:03:53.346
and he did it with a six-year-old.
他让六岁的我去做。

48
00:03:56.153 --> 00:03:58.485
[Kelly]The things that Tommy’s dad took him on,
Tommy 老爹带他做的那些动作，

49
00:03:58.697 --> 00:04:01.188
today you would have Child Protective Services
到如今看，儿童保护中心

50
00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:02.739
coming after you.
都会在身后来追诉的

51
00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:07.285
He basically took hardship and rephrased it as growth.
他本质上就是把艰难困苦，演绎为成长中的一环

52
00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:11.365
[Tommy]He was loving, but he definitely let me suffer.
我老爹很萌，不过他铁了心是要让我吃些苦的。

53
00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:15.077
The word that was in my mind was resilience.
在我心里，那个词叫做弹性。

54
00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:17.879
It seems to me one of the best gifts you can give your kid
对我而言，给子女最好的礼物，

55
00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.582
is an ability to deal with adversity.
莫过于处于逆境时的应对能力

56
00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:26.513
[Tommy] By the time I was 14 or 15,
当我14或15岁时

57
00:04:26.725 --> 00:04:30.593
there was climbs that I could do that my dad couldn’t.
有一场攀岩比赛，我可以参加，我老爹不可以

58
00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:31.972
[Dad]Tommy’s strong.
Tommy很强大的

59
00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:33.929
[Tommy]Climbing was the first thing in my life
攀岩是我生命的头等大事

60
00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:35.980
where I could stand out a little bit.
因为我可以比别人强出去一点点

61
00:04:36.193 --> 00:04:37.649
[Mom] Airight. Woo!
好棒

62
00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:41.528
[Dad]So Tommy was 16,
Tommy16岁时，

63
00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.903
and Snowbird held the Snowbird Invitational that year.
雪鸟城组织举行了一场雪鸟邀请赛

64
00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.824
[Tommy]This big climbing competition.
那是一次大型攀岩竞赛

65
00:04:47.037 --> 00:04:49.278
We thought we’d drive over there and watch the comp
我们本以为就是开车去看比赛的

66
00:04:49.498 --> 00:04:50.658
and get some autographs.
得到一些签名

67
00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:52.990
[Tommy] We just went there to be fans, really.
真是，本来准备去当粉丝的

68
00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.950
[Dad] And the day before the big competition,
结果，大赛的前一天

69
00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.786
they had a Citizens’ Comp that anybody who shows up can enter.
他们在Citizens' Comp会议上决定，任何去现场的都可以参赛

70
00:04:58.006 --> 00:05:01.169
[Tommy] So I entered that, my first competition ever.
所以，我就参加了。我的平生第一次参赛

71
00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:03.716
[Dad]Well, Tommy won.
昂，Tommy 赢了比赛

72
00:05:03.929 --> 00:05:06.261
And I don’t know if this was an official policy
我不知这是不是官方规则

73
00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:08.509
or just something they dreamt up on the spot,
还是当场他们随意的决定

74
00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:10.056
but they asked Tommy
那会儿他们问Tommy

75
00:05:10.268 --> 00:05:13.010
if he wanted to enter the World Invitational the next day.
他能否参加第二天的世界邀请赛

76
00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.686
Hello, everyone. I’m James Brown,
大家好，我是James Brown

77
00:05:14.898 --> 00:05:16.229
and welcome to Snowbird, Utah,
欢迎来到犹他州的雪球城

78
00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.397
for the International Sport Climbing Championship.
观看国际体育攀岩冠军杯赛

79
00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.566
[Presenter] Expert climbers will test their skills
专业攀岩者将运用他们的技术

80
00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:24.363
against a man-made 120-foot wall.
攀爬120英尺的人造岩体

81
00:05:24.574 --> 00:05:26.064
[Dad] There were 12 competitors.
总共有12名参赛者

82
00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:28.900
-[Tommy]The icons of climbing.
-[Dad]and it was so intimidating.
攀岩图标
很吓人

83
00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:35.994
[Tommy] Nobody had ever heard of me.
那时没人知晓我

84
00:05:36.211 --> 00:05:37.951
I was just this scrawny little kid.
我只是一个瘦弱的小孩

85
00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:40.583
I was videoing Tommy as he goes climbing up this thing.
Tommy攀爬时，我在给他录像

86
00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:47.052
[Dad] Come on, Tommy.
加油，Tommy

87
00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.925
[Dad] He got past the final roof.
他越过了最后的终点

88
00:05:54.396 --> 00:05:56.136
So Tommy’s winning.
Tommy是冠军

89
00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.936
[Man]Airight, Tommy!
Tommy，真棒

90
00:06:01.152 --> 00:06:02.312
And I started shaking.
我都发抖了

91
00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.486
I just dropped the camera.
摄像机也摔掉了下去

92
00:06:08.702 --> 00:06:10.442
I mean I completely lost it.
呃，我意思是，我整个没抓住摄像机。

93
00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:12.865
[Dad]Tommy got to the top.
Tommy到达顶端终点时

94
00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:17.165
The only climber to complete this climb.
是唯一一个完成全部攀岩的选手

95
00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:20.790
So all of a sudden,
Tommy went from nobody at all
Tommy从默默无闻

96
00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:23.042
to winner of Snowbird
变成雪鸟城的攀岩冠军

97
00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:25.294
[Mom] I mean, that was just unbelievable.
真是不可思议

98
00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.967
It changed his whole life.
完全改变了他的生命

99
00:06:28.179 --> 00:06:29.464
[KeIIy] Tommy became known
Tommy变成了

100
00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:31.546
as one of the best young climbers.
最佳的年轻攀岩家之一

101
00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:32.755
But he didn’t grow up
但，他并没有

102
00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:34.216
the way most of us do.
以我们一般成长的方式长大

103
00:06:34.436 --> 00:06:36.222
Through high school he didn’t have girlfriends.
整个高中时期，他没有女友

104
00:06:36.438 --> 00:06:39.396
He didn’t have a social life. He just went climbing.
他没有社交圈生活。他就是一个劲的攀岩

105
00:06:39.608 --> 00:06:42.065
[PA, indistinctl

106
00:06:43.737 --> 00:06:46.274
[Tommy] I was doing this series of competitions,
在一系列的攀岩竞赛中

107
00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:49.071
and I met this girl, Beth.
我遇到了Beth

108
00:06:49.284 --> 00:06:52.151
She just caught my attention totally. I was like, “Woah!”
老天，她完全吸引住我

109
00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.784
Tommy just had this really big, goofy, endearing grin.
Tommy笑容灿烂、笨拙、隐忍


110
00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.333
We both lived and breathed climbing.
我们俩都以攀岩为生命

111
00:07:00.545 --> 00:07:02.661
[KeIIy] Tommy’s this climbing savant,
Tommy有了攀岩同伴专家

112
00:07:02.881 --> 00:07:07.295
and then he meets Beth, the female version of himself.
他遇见Beth，就像遇见他自己的女性版

113
00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.046
He’s head over heels.
简直喜不自禁

114
00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.628
[Tommy] I just found ways to go wherever she was.
只要她去的地方，我都设法过去

115
00:07:11.848 --> 00:07:13.964
-OK?
-Yeah.

116
00:07:14.184 --> 00:07:16.800
[Tommy] I found out she was going to Yosemite,
我发现她要去优胜美地

117
00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.306
so I followed her out there.
就一路追随过去

118
00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:22.935
We ended up climbing a big wall together.
我们一起攀爬完成一块大岩墙

119
00:07:23.151 --> 00:07:25.267
You know, we were next to each other all the time.
是呀，我们一直并肩攀爬

120
00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:27.318
24 hours a day together.
24小时在一起

121
00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.488
[Beth]Sleeping 1,000 feet off the ground on this portaledge,
睡在离地1000英尺的半空中，在可折叠悬挂帐篷里

122
00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.032
which is like a hanging cot.
就像是悬挂式的小床

123
00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:36.452
[Tommy]  You sleep head to toe. There’s just more room that way.
如果头脚接踵的话，也还有一点空间

124
00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:38.121
So I laid down,
所以我躺下了

125
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:40.073
and she laid down the same way that I was,
她也像我一样躺下

126
00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.033
with her head at the same end.
头并头地躺下

127
00:07:42.253 --> 00:07:43.663
And I was pretty excited by this.
当时我特别激动

128
00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.748
I was like “Ooh, goodness. This is getting exciting.”
我想，老天，真是太兴奋了

129
00:07:49.386 --> 00:07:50.842
I just hadn’t been in love before,
之前我从没有爱过谁

130
00:07:51.054 --> 00:07:54.217
and I just fell hardcore, right off the bat.
那个瞬间，立刻就陷入了

131
00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:58.008
[Beth] It just clicked.
就是来电的感觉

132
00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:02.221
We had so many dreams of traveling and climbing together.
我们拥有如此多的梦想：一起旅行一起攀岩

133
00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:07.476
And then we got invited to go on a big adventure trip.
之后，我们受到邀请

134
00:08:07.696 --> 00:08:10.187
An expedition to Kyrgyzstan.
去参加在吉尔吉斯斯坦的一次野外探险旅行

135
00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:12.898
Kyrgyzstan is this beautiful, mountainous country
吉尔吉斯斯坦是个多山的美丽国家

136
00:08:13.118 --> 00:08:14.403
in Central Asia.
在亚洲中部

137
00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:18.032
We’d seen pictures from friends that had been there,
我们曾经看到过一些朋友去后拍摄的图片

138
00:08:18.248 --> 00:08:19.909
and it looked like a paradise for climbers.
对于攀岩选手，那里简直就是天堂。

139
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.867
I was a photographer working in the outdoor industry.
我是一名户外摄影家

140
00:08:23.086 --> 00:08:25.919
And this amazing opportunity came about for me
当时接到一个灰常棒的机会

141
00:08:26.131 --> 00:08:29.168
to shoot an expedition with Beth and Tommy and Jason.
与Beth、Tommy和Jason一起远行，给他们做拍摄

142
00:08:29.384 --> 00:08:31.966
We were just four young climbers looking for a big adventure
我们是四个喜欢探险的

143
00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:35.386
in a new and unusual part of the world.
喜欢在世界上新的地点、不同寻常的地点去做攀岩的年轻人

144
00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:39.011
[Tommy] We charter a helicopter into the Kara-Su Valley.
我们包了一架直升机，来到Kara-Su山谷

145
00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:41.263
Unbelievably beautiful.
美丽到难以置信

146
00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:44.061
Just felt like a dream come true,
感觉梦想成真

147
00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:45.889
out in the middle of this adventure
一边探险

148
00:08:46.109 --> 00:08:48.350
with this girl that I was totally in love with.
一边与我深爱的女孩在一起

149
00:08:49.946 --> 00:08:51.356
A week-and-a-half into our trip,
出行一周半以后的一天

150
00:08:51.573 --> 00:08:53.359
the four of us were sleeping in portaledges
我们四个正睡在悬挂式野营帐篷里时

151
00:08:53.575 --> 00:08:55.065
1,000 feet up the wall,
高度是在岩壁的1000英尺处

152
00:08:55.285 --> 00:08:58.448
-and we wake up to gunshots...
-[Gunshot]
我们被枪声惊醒

153
00:08:58.663 --> 00:09:00.619
...these piercing, close gunshots.
子弹的穿透声，越来越近

154
00:09:00.832 --> 00:09:02.242
[Gunshots]

155
00:09:02.459 --> 00:09:04.415
The bullets hitting the wall right between our portaledges.
子弹击中了我们几个悬挂帐篷之间的岩石

156
00:09:04.627 --> 00:09:05.867
We’re sitting there like,
我们坐在那里

157
00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:07.702
“Oh, my God, we’re getting shot at.”
老天，难道我们要被打中吗

158
00:09:07.922 --> 00:09:09.503
And you can’t run away. You can’t do anything.
可是，既无法逃跑，也无法做任何其它事


159
00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:11.547
We’re just sitting ducks up here.
就像别人的靶子，只能坐在那儿

160
00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.048
We look down, and you could see these figures.
我们往下看，可以看到这些人影

161
00:09:15.263 --> 00:09:17.925
[Tommy] These guys waving at us to come down.
他们朝我们挥手示意我们下去

162
00:09:18.141 --> 00:09:19.927
[Beth]We rappelled down to the ground.
我们靠绳索下降

163
00:09:20.143 --> 00:09:24.182
[Tommy] We’re encountered by four guys, heavily armed.
下去以后，见到四个全副武装的人

164
00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:25.978
[John] They took us to our base camp.
他们把我们弄到我们的攀岩大本营

165
00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:27.647
[Jason] All of our tents were cut open.
我们的帐篷全部被割开

166
00:09:27.859 --> 00:09:29.565
A lot of our food was splayed around the meadow.
许多我们的食品被撒落在四周的草地上

167
00:09:29.778 --> 00:09:31.609
They had us start hiding our camp.
他们让我们把帐篷藏起来

168
00:09:31.821 --> 00:09:35.780
And so suddenly, it hits us, we’re hostages right now.
这时我们才醒悟到，自己是人质

169
00:09:45.376 --> 00:09:46.991
[Beth] Later, we learned that these guys
之后，我们知道这些人

170
00:09:47.212 --> 00:09:49.669
were part of the Islamic Movement of Uzbekistan,
是乌兹别克斯坦的伊斯兰运动组织成员

171
00:09:49.881 --> 00:09:52.748
these rebels that wanted to overthrow the government.
他们目标是推翻政府

172
00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:57.252
[John] We were caught up in this battle
我们被卷入这场

173
00:09:57.472 --> 00:10:00.305
between these rebels and the Kyrgyz military.
吉尔吉斯军队与叛军之间的争战

174
00:10:01.684 --> 00:10:02.890
[Tommy] All of a sudden,
突然之间

175
00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:04.639
Kyrgyz military helicopters started to fly over,
吉尔吉斯军队的直升机在头顶盘旋

176
00:10:04.854 --> 00:10:07.470
soldiers show up on the hillside,
山坡上也有士兵出现

177
00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.851
-and this battle breaks out. 争战开始
-[Gunfire]

178
00:10:10.068 --> 00:10:12.684
The rebels start pointing their guns at us, yelling. “Hide!”
叛军用枪指着我们吼道：躲起来

179
00:10:12.904 --> 00:10:14.815
Then we dive in these trees.
我们就躲避到树林里

180
00:10:15.031 --> 00:10:17.647
[John] The rebels had taken a Kyrgyz soldier hostage.
叛军也抓吉尔吉斯士兵的人质

181
00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:19.152
They took the other captive.
他们把抓到的其他俘虏

182
00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:20.984
And they just shot him in the head.
在脑袋上直接给一枪

183
00:10:21.204 --> 00:10:23.365
[Gunshot]

184
00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:25.367
I just remember shaking uncontrollably
记得我那时，不由自主地颤抖

185
00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:27.869
and Tommy just holding me as tight as he could.
Tommy紧紧地抱着我

186
00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:30.418
Are they just going to kill us next?
他们会不会下次就枪杀我们？

187
00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.996
[Distant gunfire]

188
00:10:33.216 --> 00:10:35.878
[Tommy] Once it’s dark, the gunfire dies down.
天黑以后，枪击声消退了

189
00:10:36.094 --> 00:10:39.632
And the rebels start marching us through the mountains.
叛军押着我们穿过山脉

190
00:10:43.977 --> 00:10:48.220
It’s four rebels, the four of us.
叛军是四个，我们也是四个

191
00:10:48.439 --> 00:10:50.976
It’s really cold. We’re 11,000 feet in elevation.
超级冷。我们在海拔11000英尺的高地上

192
00:10:51.192 --> 00:10:52.682
We don’t have warm clothes.
没有暖和的衣服

193
00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:54.358
We don’t have any food.
也没有任何食物

194
00:10:54.571 --> 00:10:57.654
[Beth] We had no idea where we were going.
我们都不知道会去哪里

195
00:10:57.866 --> 00:11:00.198
[John] We would hike through the night,
要徒步穿过黑夜

196
00:11:01.828 --> 00:11:04.740
and then during the day, they would hide us.
天明以后，他们就藏起我们

197
00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:08.744
[Beth] They hid us in the craziest spots.
他们把我们藏身在一些难以想象的地方

198
00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:11.042
[Tommy] Burying us in holes in the ground
比如地下的洞穴里

199
00:11:11.254 --> 00:11:14.417
so that we wouldn’t be seen by the military.
这样政府军就不会看到我们

200
00:11:14.632 --> 00:11:16.293
[John] This went on for six days.
就这样过了六天

201
00:11:16.509 --> 00:11:20.093
[Beth] Day two or three, hunger really started to set in.
从第二或第三天开始，饥饿就击倒了我们

202
00:11:20.305 --> 00:11:23.092
[Tommy] You know, we’re sort of just wasting away.
你明白的，我们变得特消瘦

203
00:11:23.308 --> 00:11:25.594
[Beth]  I thought they’re taking us back to their base
我以为他们要把我们带回基地

204
00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.472
or they’re taking us somewhere, there’s a purpose to this.
或者带到什么地方，总之有一个目的地

205
00:11:28.688 --> 00:11:30.303
[John] Finally, we realized
最后，我们意识到

206
00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.935
they were leading us in a giant circle.
他们就是带着我们兜了一个大圈子

207
00:11:33.151 --> 00:11:36.234
Like, these guys clearly don’t have a plan.
就是说，这些人根本就没有啥计划。

208
00:11:36.446 --> 00:11:39.859
Jason and John started to scheme about how we could get away.
Jason 和John开始思量该怎么逃脱

209
00:11:40.074 --> 00:11:41.905
I mean, things were getting super desperate.
我意思是，情形变得超级绝望

210
00:11:42.118 --> 00:11:44.734
They were ready to take matters into their own hands.
他们预备把形势掌控到自己手上

211
00:11:44.954 --> 00:11:47.286
At one point, two of our captors left.
在某个地点，抓捕我们的人，其中有两个离开了。

212
00:11:47.498 --> 00:11:49.409
-We never saw them again.
-[Gunshots]
自后再也未见过他们

213
00:11:49.626 --> 00:11:53.039
We found out later that they got killed.
然后才发现他们被打死了

214
00:11:53.254 --> 00:11:55.961
On our sixth night of captivity,
所以在被抓捕后的第六天

215
00:11:56.174 --> 00:11:58.540
the two captors that were remaining with us
剩下两个抓捕我们的人

216
00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.796
decided that one of them would go in one direction
决定其中一个人应该

217
00:12:01.012 --> 00:12:02.172
to try and get some food
沿着一个方向去找吃的

218
00:12:02.388 --> 00:12:04.549
and then we would head off with the other one.
我们这些人，就和另一个抓捕者一起走。

219
00:12:09.562 --> 00:12:12.053
[John] So we get left alone with the one rebel,
那时，押解我们的就只有一个人了

220
00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:14.309
climbing up this cliff side.
他把我们押着爬上悬崖边。

221
00:12:14.525 --> 00:12:17.733
We were comfortable on the terrain, and he was not.
我们是很习惯这种悬崖地形的，而叛军不是

222
00:12:17.946 --> 00:12:21.438
If we’re going to escape, this is the opportunity.
如果企图逃脱，这是绝好机会

223
00:12:21.658 --> 00:12:23.273
[Tommy] Jason and John decided
Jason 和John 开始决定

224
00:12:23.493 --> 00:12:27.202
they would try and push our remaining captor off this cliff
他们想把这个留守的抓捕者推下悬崖

225
00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:28.744
and then run away.
然后逃跑

226
00:12:28.957 --> 00:12:30.822
[Jason]John and I were trying to look for a point
Jason 和我开始找合适的地点

227
00:12:31.042 --> 00:12:32.031
that we could throw him off.
让我们可以推他下悬崖

228
00:12:32.252 --> 00:12:34.994
[John]But we kept going and kept going.
但我们一直走啊走

229
00:12:35.213 --> 00:12:37.579
We just couldn’t quite push him.
没法一下子就推下他

230
00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.381
[Tommy] As we got to the top,
等我们到达山顶

231
00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:43.676
I realized that our opportunity was going to be over.
我觉得我们的机会已经过去了

232
00:12:49.727 --> 00:12:53.595
And I decided that this was what I had to do.
因此我认为这事应该由我去做

233
00:12:53.815 --> 00:12:57.524
I had to go and I needed to push this guy off this cliff
我想跑走，所以就需要把他推下悬崖

234
00:12:57.735 --> 00:12:59.191
in order to save our lives.
这样我们才能得救

235
00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:02.237
Tommy came over to me at this point, and he said,
Tommy 就过来问我

236
00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:04.063
“Do you think I should do this?”
“你觉得是不是我应该去做？”

237
00:13:04.284 --> 00:13:06.275
I was thinking, “Yes, no, yes, no.”
我想，是的，不是，是的，不是

238
00:13:06.494 --> 00:13:08.450
So I just didn’t say anything.
却一个字也没有说出来

239
00:13:08.663 --> 00:13:12.952
[Tommy] I took that as that she would be OK with it.
我把Beth的沉默看成是她默许这个事

240
00:13:15.253 --> 00:13:18.916
So I just ran up behind him
所以就跑在叛军解押者的后面

241
00:13:19.132 --> 00:13:24.217
and I put one hand on his back and grabbed his gun strap.
往他后背推了一掌，同时抓住他的枪带

242
00:13:24.429 --> 00:13:27.717
And my other hand went on his chest
我另一只手伸向他的胸部

243
00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:30.173
and I just gave a push...
推了一下

244
00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.471
...to send him flying off this cliff.
把他推翻飞下悬崖

245
00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:44.778
We saw him hit a ledge,
我们看见他摔倒在伸出的一块平整岩石上

246
00:13:44.991 --> 00:13:47.983
bounce off of it, and just fall out of sight into the darkness.
被重新弹出，然后就摔进黑暗，再也看不到了

247
00:13:51.456 --> 00:13:52.946
[Beth]
Tommy completely broke down,
Tommy整个人都崩溃了

248
00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:55.578
had his head in his arms and he was crying.
头埋进胳膊开始哭

249
00:13:55.793 --> 00:13:57.624
[Tommy] I couldn’t believe what I had just done.
无法相信自己的所作所为

250
00:13:57.837 --> 00:13:59.543
I had just killed somebody.
无法相信自己杀了人

251
00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:03.965
The whole world came crashing down on me all at once.
片刻之间，整个世界都压倒了我

252
00:14:04.177 --> 00:14:06.919
[Beth] We were all trying to reassure him and say that,
我们大家都使劲肯定Tommy的行为 

253
00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:09.754
“You’re not a bad person, you just saved our lives.”
都说，你不是坏人，是你才救了我们

254
00:14:09.974 --> 00:14:11.589
[Tommy] They really tried to comfort me.
大家都尝试着安慰我

255
00:14:11.809 --> 00:14:13.845
But there was a sense of urgency that we better get going,
但，当时最紧迫的是需要跑出来

256
00:14:14.062 --> 00:14:17.395
because we didn’t know if the other captor was gonna show up.
因为我们不知道那个另外的叛军解押是否会出现

257
00:14:17.607 --> 00:14:19.848
[John] We knew from hiking in earlier
早先在徒步探险时，我们知道

258
00:14:20.068 --> 00:14:23.231
where there was a military outpost we could try and run to.
有一支政府警戒分队（在附近），我们可以跑去求助

259
00:14:23.446 --> 00:14:25.858
[Beth] So even on almost no food for six days,
这样，尽管饿了六天

260
00:14:26.074 --> 00:14:27.280
adrenaline kicked in.
肾上腺还是刺激了身体

261
00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:28.948
[Jason]
So we ran for four hours.
我们因此一口气跑了四个小时

262
00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.025
Through the darkness down this valley.
穿过黑暗，下到山谷

263
00:14:31.245 --> 00:14:33.782
[Beth] We were greeted by this man yelling at us with this gun.
之后有一个人用枪指着我们，对我们大喊大叫

264
00:14:33.998 --> 00:14:36.831
[John] Throw up our hands, start yelling that we’re Americans.
我们举起手，也开始大喊，说我们是美国人

265
00:14:37.043 --> 00:14:39.159
[Beth] And luckily, it was the Kyrgyz army.
幸运的是，这是吉尔吉斯斯坦部队

266
00:14:39.379 --> 00:14:42.371
This huge wave of relief came over us.
获释的巨大喜悦汹涌而至

267
00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:47.004
This horrible situation that we had been in was over.
我们经历的恐怖状况总算过去

268
00:14:48.554 --> 00:14:52.388
They gave us food and water, military fatigues.
他们给了我们这些逃难者一些东西吃喝

269
00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.761
And then we got helicoptered out from there.
再之后，我们乘直升机离开那里。

270
00:15:00.775 --> 00:15:03.608
[Presenter]  From our studios in New York, here’s Jane Pauley.
Jane Pauley 在纽约工作室报道

271
00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.903
[Jane] Four young Americans face a life or death choice,
四位年轻的美国人面对生死选择

272
00:15:07.115 --> 00:15:11.233
with the ultimate question, to kill or be killed?
终极问题是，杀人还是被杀

273
00:15:11.452 --> 00:15:14.944
[Tommy] When we got home, there was this crazy media circus.
回到家中，狂热的媒体包围过来

274
00:15:15.164 --> 00:15:17.871
You guys are walking with this captor
你们和这个抓捕人一起

275
00:15:18.084 --> 00:15:19.915
on a very rocky cliff.
走过岩石丛生的悬崖

276
00:15:20.128 --> 00:15:21.334
Tell me what you did, Tommy.
Tommy，和我说说发生了什么

277
00:15:21.546 --> 00:15:24.504
We just ended up pushing the guy.
我们就是把他推下去了

278
00:15:24.715 --> 00:15:26.171
-You pushed him over the cliff.
-Yeah.
你把他推下了悬崖 ----- 是

279
00:15:26.384 --> 00:15:28.249
What happened at that moment when you realized,
那一刻，当你意识到

280
00:15:28.469 --> 00:15:30.505
I’ve actually done this, I’ve killed somebody?
我真的这么做了，我杀死了人，到底发生了什么？

281
00:15:30.721 --> 00:15:34.009
I thought that I was an evil person. I said to Beth,
我对Beth说，觉得自己是个罪人

282
00:15:34.225 --> 00:15:37.638
“How can you love me after I did something like this?”
这件事后，你还能爱我吗？

283
00:15:37.854 --> 00:15:39.685
And, uh...
唉

284
00:15:41.816 --> 00:15:43.181
[Dad] After Kyrgyzstan,
从吉尔吉斯斯坦事件以后

285
00:15:43.401 --> 00:15:45.608
Tommy had tremendous personality changes.
Tommy的性格大变

286
00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.651
Speaking so softly.
说话变得轻声

287
00:15:47.864 --> 00:15:51.698
I was like, what is inside me that allowed me to do this?
我在想，自己内心里面到底是什么允许自己这么做的？

288
00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:56.073
Just an entirely different person.
完全是一个不同的人


289
00:16:37.622 --> 00:16:38.782
[John Long] Yosemite is known
优胜美地

290
00:16:38.998 --> 00:16:41.831
as the Mecca of world rock climbing.
对于世界攀岩者来说，是可仰慕的朝圣地

291
00:16:44.879 --> 00:16:48.747
And the crown jewel of this Mecca is El Capitan.
而朝圣地的皇冠珍宝是El Capitan岩壁

292
00:16:50.301 --> 00:16:54.840
It’s just this iconic 3,000 foot high monolith.
它是标志性级别的3000英尺高的单体花岗岩

293
00:16:55.056 --> 00:16:57.092
When you see that thing for the first time,
若是第一次看见它，

294
00:16:57.308 --> 00:16:59.890
it takes your breath away.
你会摒住呼吸

295
00:17:00.102 --> 00:17:04.687
The steepest, blankest, most forlorn...
最陡峭、最荒芜、最孤独的

296
00:17:04.899 --> 00:17:06.935
impressive part of El Cap
El Capitan 的那一处

297
00:17:07.151 --> 00:17:09.107
is the Dawn Wall.
就是the Dawn Wall (黎明墙）

298
00:17:11.322 --> 00:17:14.064
People have done a handful of free climbs up El Cap
人们曾经无数次尝试徒手攀登El Capitan

299
00:17:14.283 --> 00:17:16.274
to the right and to the left.
从右侧或左侧

300
00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:21.704
But the Dawn Wall has never been climbed.
但，黎明墙，至今无人徒手攀爬上去过。

301
00:17:21.916 --> 00:17:25.579
Just the sheer magnitude of blank rock on the thing,
纯粹是巨大的一块大岩石

302
00:17:25.795 --> 00:17:28.127
it just looks impossible.
完全是一种不可能

303
00:17:29.423 --> 00:17:32.039
Until Tommy CaIdwell came along,
直到Tommy Caldwell攀登以前

304
00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.094
nobody had actually considered trying it.
此前，没有人真正考虑徒手攀爬过

305
00:17:36.305 --> 00:17:40.014
If Tommy and his partner Kevin can actually do this,
如果Tommy和他的搭档Kevin 可以做到

306
00:17:40.226 --> 00:17:45.516
it will be the most continuously difficult rock climb ever done.
那意味着，人类终于把这一块难以克服的岩石给制服了

307
00:17:47.733 --> 00:17:50.099
Nothing else is even close to it.
不过从目前说，还无人接近这个目标

308
00:17:52.488 --> 00:17:54.524
[Tommyl It’s December 27th,
12月27日

309
00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:58.403
and we’re planning on heading up for like two weeks plus.
我们已经花两周多时间，计划出发了

310
00:17:59.328 --> 00:18:01.068
We’ll see.
我们要等看结果

311
00:18:01.289 --> 00:18:04.747
The goal is climb it in a single push,
目标是一次性攀爬

312
00:18:04.959 --> 00:18:07.041
which means we’re going to leave the ground,
换言之，我们从离开地面算起

313
00:18:07.253 --> 00:18:08.993
live on the wall,
中间住在岩壁上

314
00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:13.919
and not come down until we’re done.
直到成功登顶后，方可下岩

315
00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:17.960
[Kevin] We’re going for it.
我们准备出发

316
00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.886
I’m nervous.
有点儿紧张

317
00:18:20.099 --> 00:18:24.468
We’ve put in so much work leading up to this moment.
为了这一刻，已经准备了许久的工作

318
00:18:24.687 --> 00:18:27.599
There’s nothing left to do but take a couple deep breaths
别的都可以了，只需深吸一口气

319
00:18:27.815 --> 00:18:29.180
and start climbing.
开始攀登

320
00:18:29.942 --> 00:18:32.433
Day one. 第一日

321
00:18:32.653 --> 00:18:33.984
Yup.对

322
00:18:36.157 --> 00:18:37.522
This is going to be awesome.
很惊人呐

323
00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.407
[Long] The Dawn Wall itself is 3,000 feet tall.
黎明墙本身有3千英尺高

324
00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:47.790
The route that they think they have figured out
他们思考过的可能途径

325
00:18:48.002 --> 00:18:51.836
is comprised of 32 individual pitches.
总共有32个独立绳距

326
00:18:52.048 --> 00:18:56.838
Each pitch is its own challenge,like the stages of a race.
每一个绳距都是挑战，就是像进入比赛场地

327
00:18:59.555 --> 00:19:03.468
A pitch is a rope-length long, about 150 feet or so.
一个绳距的意思是，大约150尺长短，就是一根绳子的大概长度

328
00:19:03.684 --> 00:19:05.049
And ends of the ledge
在（绳距的）末尾平台部分

329
00:19:05.269 --> 00:19:08.511
are a natural resting place on the rock.
是岩石上天然的休息处

330
00:19:08.731 --> 00:19:10.471
[Tommy] Yeah, man. Good work.
哥们，厉害。干的棒

331
00:19:10.691 --> 00:19:12.056
[Long] When you end the pitch,
当你完成一个绳距时

332
00:19:12.276 --> 00:19:14.312
you anchor yourself to the wall...
就可以在岩墙上挂锚

333
00:19:14.528 --> 00:19:17.861
[kevin] One down, thirty-something to go.
一个再下去，大概三十尺左右

334
00:19:18.074 --> 00:19:21.066
[Long] ...and hold the rope or belay as your partner comes up.
然后抓住绳子，或者栓在系绳栓上，等待同伴上来


335
00:19:22.787 --> 00:19:24.823
Once you’ve both done that pitch without falling,
如果两个攀岩者都没有失手，完成一个绳距后

336
00:19:25.039 --> 00:19:27.075
you can move on to the next pitch.
方可继续下一个绳距

337
00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:31.325
When you’re free-climbing,
如果你是徒手抱石攀岩

338
00:19:31.545 --> 00:19:33.285
you’re using your hands and feet
你需要用到双手与双脚

339
00:19:33.506 --> 00:19:35.838
to climb the natural features on the rock
攀爬岩石上自然的裂缝

340
00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:38.666
without any assistance from the rope.
并不依赖绳子的任何辅助

341
00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:41.510
-[Kevin]Good job.
-[Tommy]Yeah, man.
真棒，是的，哥们

342
00:19:41.722 --> 00:19:44.304
[Long] You take turns leading each pitch
双方换位攀爬绳距

343
00:19:44.517 --> 00:19:47.884
placing protection in the cracks to catch you in case you fall.
在岩缝中安置保护装置，用以防止摔落

344
00:19:49.397 --> 00:19:51.604
[Tommy] Yeah, come on. You got it.
加油，哥们你行的

345
00:19:51.816 --> 00:19:53.681
Ugh! Oh! 糟

346
00:19:56.862 --> 00:19:58.898
[Tommy] If you fall, 一旦摔落

347
00:19:59.115 --> 00:20:03.154
you just go back down to the beginning of that pitch,
就需要退回到那个绳距的原点

348
00:20:03.369 --> 00:20:05.985
and then the other guy tries it.
等另一位尝试

349
00:20:06.205 --> 00:20:08.036
[Long] They have a certain number of pitches
他们有一串绳距

350
00:20:08.249 --> 00:20:10.035
they’re trying to get through each day
每天要完成一些

351
00:20:10.251 --> 00:20:12.913
to stay on track to finish this climb.
留在攀爬途径上做完本次攀爬

352
00:20:13.129 --> 00:20:16.667
The first few pitches are relatively easy.
开头的几个绳距比较容易

353
00:20:16.882 --> 00:20:19.123
But as you get higher on the wall...
但当攀爬越高

354
00:20:22.346 --> 00:20:24.712
...the wall gets steeper,
岩壁越陡峭

355
00:20:25.808 --> 00:20:27.890
the holes get smaller,
（岩点）石洞越小

356
00:20:29.145 --> 00:20:31.852
and the climbing gets way more difficult.
攀岩的困难程度就越大

357
00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:39.352
[Kevin] It’s hard to articulate
很难表达清楚

358
00:20:39.572 --> 00:20:41.984
the level of detail that’s required.
所需的具体水准

359
00:20:44.618 --> 00:20:48.110
You can’t make any mistake in where you grab the hold
当你抓抱住岩石时，不能有任何差错

360
00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:51.037
and how you place your toe.
还要明了怎样安放自己的脚趾位置

361
00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.163
You’re pushing and pulling as hard as you possibly can,
竭尽全力去推和拉

362
00:20:55.379 --> 00:20:57.836
always on the verge of slipping off.
永远都在坠落的边缘

363
00:21:02.094 --> 00:21:03.800
Argh! 啊

364
00:21:04.013 --> 00:21:05.594
[Tommy] Oh, no! 天呐

365
00:21:05.806 --> 00:21:08.343
-[Kevin]Oh!
-[Tommy]Oh, foot slip.
脚滑

366
00:21:10.436 --> 00:21:13.223
[Kevin] We climb all day into the night,
我们从白天爬到晚上

367
00:21:13.439 --> 00:21:17.227
trying the same pitch until we both do it.
在同一个绳距上各自尝试，相互完成

368
00:21:24.492 --> 00:21:25.948
Come on, Tommy!
加油，Tommy

369
00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:29.360
Come on!
加油

370
00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.156
[Tommy] Man, I’m getting tired.
哥们，真累了。

371
00:21:34.376 --> 00:21:36.367
[Kevin] Tommy is just a man possessed.
Tommy 这个人很执着

372
00:21:36.587 --> 00:21:38.748
Come on. Finish this.
加油，完成它

373
00:21:40.216 --> 00:21:41.547
Yeah, come on.
对，加油

374
00:21:43.052 --> 00:21:44.383
Yeah, man. 对，哥们

375
00:21:44.595 --> 00:21:47.257
Yee-hoo! 啊哈

376
00:21:47.473 --> 00:21:48.804
And I’m just trying to keep up.
我尽力保持住

377
00:21:49.016 --> 00:21:50.677
[Tommy] You got it, Kevin. Come on!
Kevin，你完成了，加油

378
00:21:50.893 --> 00:21:53.885
Come on! Come on! Come on! 加油

379
00:21:54.104 --> 00:21:55.969
Yeah, that was awesome, dude.
啊，真棒

380
00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:58.101
[Kevin] Thank God I didn’t fall.
感谢上帝，这次没掉下来

381
00:21:59.026 --> 00:22:00.232
[Tommy] Nice, man. 棒

382
00:22:00.444 --> 00:22:02.435
[Long] When you’re trying a big wall like this,
当你尝试这样的大岩壁时

383
00:22:02.655 --> 00:22:04.020
the work does not end
事儿是没完没了的

384
00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.822
once the climbing is done at the end of the day.
每一天完成攀爬以后

385
00:22:07.034 --> 00:22:09.901
You’ve got to haul up hundreds of pounds of gear,
就需要把几百磅重的器械拉上去

386
00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:11.985
set up portaledges...
架起悬空帐篷

387
00:22:12.206 --> 00:22:16.245
[Tommy] This seems pretty good. Pretty flat, even, I would say.
瞅瞅，看起来挺棒。还挺平

388
00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.291
[Long]
...and gag down some food.
然后吞吃一些食物

389
00:22:18.504 --> 00:22:21.496
[Tommy] I actually brought a bag of kale on the wall
事实上，我带上去了一袋子的甘蓝

390
00:22:21.715 --> 00:22:24.297
to put it in our burritos. Mmh!
可以放在卷饼一起吃

391
00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.882
This is the hardest thing you could ever do on your fingers,
这是你可以用自己手指完成的最难的事儿了

392
00:22:33.102 --> 00:22:34.638
climbing this route.
要完成这个途径

393
00:22:34.854 --> 00:22:36.640
It’s just grabbing razor blades.
就仿佛是去抓住剃刀刀片

394
00:22:36.856 --> 00:22:39.814
I tape up any wounds with Neosporin for healing.
我用Neosporin消炎膏包扎伤口

395
00:22:40.025 --> 00:22:42.892
Then I wake up probably twice in the night and reapply.
夜里可能需要醒两次重新上药

396
00:22:43.112 --> 00:22:46.479
Getting pretty obsessed with my lips.
嘴唇也超级难受

397
00:22:46.699 --> 00:22:48.906
[Long] Then you’ve got to hope you can get a little sleep.
你才希望能睡个好觉时

398
00:22:49.118 --> 00:22:52.861
The next day is going to be more of the same, but harder.
其实第二天将会差不多，还愈发艰难

399
00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.162
And it’s going to go on day after day,
天天如此

400
00:22:55.374 --> 00:22:58.241
two weeks, three weeks. Nobody knows.
两周，三周，没人知道（多久可以完成）

401
00:23:10.598 --> 00:23:12.554
[Tommy] After Kyrgyzstan,
吉尔吉斯斯坦事件以后

402
00:23:13.976 --> 00:23:16.558
we’re trying to absorb what had happened.
我们一直想忍受住发生的经过

403
00:23:19.148 --> 00:23:21.810
Beth is really traumatized.
Beth 饱受心灵创伤

404
00:23:22.026 --> 00:23:24.517
[Beth]I started to have nightmares and couldn’t sleep.
开始连着做噩梦，无法入眠

405
00:23:24.737 --> 00:23:28.150
I did not want to be separated from Tommy at that point.
我不希望在那个时刻离开Tommy

406
00:23:28.365 --> 00:23:31.232
[Tommy] Beth and I are bonded at the hip. I’m her rock.
Beth和我在同一险境，我就是她的岩石

407
00:23:31.452 --> 00:23:32.658
We go to church a few times.
我们一起上教堂好几次

408
00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:34.531
We hadn’t been to church in ten years.
过去十年间，我们都没有去过教堂

409
00:23:34.747 --> 00:23:37.079
We’re just searching. We’re like, what does this mean?
我们在探究，这到底是为什么

410
00:23:37.291 --> 00:23:38.576
We go to a therapist.
后来去看了一位心理治疗专家

411
00:23:38.792 --> 00:23:41.033
It’s like nobody knows how to deal with this situation.
貌似没有人知道怎样才能更好面对这种状态

412
00:23:42.796 --> 00:23:44.661
I think my way of dealing with it was
我想我自己的面对方式是

413
00:23:44.882 --> 00:23:48.670
you just get back on that horse and go climb again.
再次回到攀岩

414
00:23:51.347 --> 00:23:53.463
This has always been my safe place,
它一直是我的安全伞

415
00:23:53.682 --> 00:23:55.673
my way to deal with life.
是我面对生活的路途

416
00:23:59.939 --> 00:24:02.476
I didn’t know what to think about Kyrgyzstan.
我不知道怎样去思考吉尔吉斯斯坦事件

417
00:24:03.984 --> 00:24:05.690
Part of me was feeling kind of empowered.
部分的自我，感受到某种神授

418
00:24:05.903 --> 00:24:08.019
I was like, when the shit really hit the fan,
就像是，如果真的麻烦上头时

419
00:24:08.238 --> 00:24:10.445
I was able to do what needed to be done
也不得不去做应当做的事

420
00:24:10.658 --> 00:24:12.398
to get us out of there.
把自己救出困境

421
00:24:12.618 --> 00:24:14.609
[Beth] Tommy jumped right back into climbing,
Tommy 很快就回到攀岩

422
00:24:14.828 --> 00:24:17.740
and slowly we got back into our groove.
慢慢地，我们回到了常规

423
00:24:17.957 --> 00:24:20.619
[Tommy] We’re both professional rock climbers,
我们俩都是职业攀岩者

424
00:24:20.834 --> 00:24:23.826
doing these really cool climbs all over the place.
在许多地方完成了这些酷酷的攀爬

425
00:24:24.046 --> 00:24:26.753
[Beth] He started setting these lofty goals.
他开始设立宏大的理想

426
00:24:26.966 --> 00:24:29.799
[Tommy] Trying to climb harder and harder routes.
试图攀爬那些难而又难的路径

427
00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.501
And then, about a year after Kyrgyzstan,
从吉尔吉斯斯坦回来的一年后

428
00:24:32.721 --> 00:24:34.803
we were remodeling this tiny little cabin.
我们重建了这个林中小木屋

429
00:24:37.184 --> 00:24:42.304
And Tommy was using his parent’s old table saw.
Tommy 还用到了他父母的老桌锯

430
00:24:42.523 --> 00:24:44.855
[Dad] Tommy did something that you should never do,
Tommy做的这件事，你永远都不该去做

431
00:24:45.067 --> 00:24:47.353
which is he tried to pull a small piece of wood
他把一小块木头放进锯子里

432
00:24:47.569 --> 00:24:49.275
through the table saw.
据来据去

433
00:24:49.488 --> 00:24:50.944
If the blade catches on the wood,
当锯子刀片碰到木头时

434
00:24:51.156 --> 00:24:53.397
it sucks your hand right back into the blade.
直接就把手指卷进去了

435
00:24:54.535 --> 00:24:55.820
I heard Tommy scream,
我听到Tommy的惨叫

436
00:24:56.036 --> 00:24:57.367
“I fucking cut off my finger, I cut off my finger.”
我切到手指了，我切断手指了

437
00:24:57.579 --> 00:24:59.490
Completely cut his finger off instantly.
瞬间就割断了手指

438
00:24:59.707 --> 00:25:01.038
It was over in the bushes.
手指飞到了草丛

439
00:25:01.250 --> 00:25:03.206
Beth finds the finger laying in this pile of sawdust.
Beth 在锯木屑中找到断指

440
00:25:03.419 --> 00:25:05.751
We throw it on ice, drive to the hospital.
我们用冰裹住，开车去医院

441
00:25:05.963 --> 00:25:08.750
My dad comes in, and he’s like,“You have to fix his finger.”
我老爹进来时，还在念叨，你要把手指带上

442
00:25:08.966 --> 00:25:11.548
[Beth]And so for two weeks, they tried to reattach it.
随后的两周，他们都在设法断指再接

443
00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:13.296
[Tommy]
Three different surgeries.
三位外科大夫

444
00:25:13.512 --> 00:25:16.094
But it became apparent that the finger wasn’t going to survive.
可是，很明显，手指没有能存活下来

445
00:25:19.560 --> 00:25:21.516
This one doctor who was a climber
其中一个大夫自己就是攀岩者

446
00:25:21.729 --> 00:25:24.095
came in and told Tommy that he was going to have to
走进了告诉Tommy说，他需要

447
00:25:24.314 --> 00:25:25.770
come up with a new career now.
从此开始找新的工作

448
00:25:25.983 --> 00:25:29.692
There’s no way he was going to make it as a climber any longer.
他再也不可能回到攀岩这件事

449
00:25:30.529 --> 00:25:32.565
Oh, that was...天呐 ... 这也

450
00:25:32.781 --> 00:25:35.523
either the wrong thing or the right thing to say,
也不知该说是对还是错

451
00:25:35.743 --> 00:25:37.574
because it sure fired him up.
因为这一下子就激怒了Tommy

452
00:25:37.786 --> 00:25:39.367
I was like. ‘Tuck that guy!
我想，见鬼去吧，他

453
00:25:39.580 --> 00:25:41.445
“He doesn’t know what I’m capable of.”
他根本不知道我擅长什么

454
00:25:41.665 --> 00:25:44.702
[Beth] I remember the first time he tried to climb.
我还记得他后来的第一次攀爬

455
00:25:44.918 --> 00:25:47.034
Good, Tommy.
挺棒，Tommy

456
00:25:48.589 --> 00:25:51.251
He was like, “Whoa!”
他，呃， 就像，天呐

457
00:25:51.467 --> 00:25:52.673
You know, it’s going to be hard.
你明白，真的很难

458
00:25:52.885 --> 00:25:54.091
Good job, sweetie.
宝贝，干的好

459
00:25:54.303 --> 00:25:56.089
[Long] When I heard he cut his finger off, I go,
我听到他割断手指后，我就过去了

460
00:25:56.305 --> 00:25:58.466
“Well, so much for Tommy CaIdwell.”
哎，够他受的了。

461
00:25:58.682 --> 00:25:59.922
The grip in climbing is,
攀岩的握力

462
00:26:00.142 --> 00:26:02.383
you wrap your thumb over your finger like that
是需要你用拇指搭在其它手指上，像这样

463
00:26:02.603 --> 00:26:04.139
and pull down on the little edges,
然后去抓住小小的（石头）边缘

464
00:26:04.354 --> 00:26:08.472
and if there’s no finger there, the physics are all wrong.
但如果没有这个指头，物理上的原则都不一样了

465
00:26:11.445 --> 00:26:13.606
I don’t know about that.
我真不知道这个

466
00:26:13.822 --> 00:26:16.063
[Tommy] Everybody around me, except for Beth and my parents,
周围所有的人，除了Beth和我父母

467
00:26:16.283 --> 00:26:20.242
looked at me and they’re like,“He’s done. That’s so sad.”
他们看着我，就像说，他完了，真可悲

468
00:26:20.454 --> 00:26:22.035
I knew it wasn’t going to be easy.
我明白这不容易

469
00:26:22.247 --> 00:26:24.408
But ever since Kyrgyzstan,
但自从吉尔吉斯斯坦事件后

470
00:26:24.625 --> 00:26:26.161
I just have this fire in me
我心里就有一团火

471
00:26:26.376 --> 00:26:31.120
that is different than anything I’ve had before.
和我以前感受的都全然不同

472
00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:34.832
[Dad] He had all these jars of rice and beans and gravel.
他有一堆盛满米粒，豆子或沙砾的瓶子

473
00:26:35.052 --> 00:26:37.259
He’s supposed to jam that nub of a finger in there.
他要把断指的根部扎进瓶子

474
00:26:37.471 --> 00:26:39.177
[Tommy] I just abused the thing
我就是滥用这些东西

475
00:26:39.389 --> 00:26:41.550
to retrain the nerves, to toughen them up.
要重新训练神经，和强壮神经

476
00:26:43.894 --> 00:26:46.886
Those six days of captivity in Kyrgyzstan
在吉尔吉斯斯坦的六天

477
00:26:48.190 --> 00:26:51.728
were so profoundly painful.
痛苦如此深重

478
00:26:54.988 --> 00:26:57.229
At first, I felt overwhelmed
开始时，我感觉到

479
00:26:57.449 --> 00:27:01.863
with fear and fatigue and hunger.
被恐惧、疲劳和饥饿击倒

480
00:27:02.079 --> 00:27:05.617
But at some point, I felt something come over me,
可是，在某一点是，却感觉身体里有某种东西

481
00:27:05.833 --> 00:27:08.040
this reserve of energy,
能量的保存

482
00:27:09.253 --> 00:27:10.868
this confidence.
这一种自信

483
00:27:11.088 --> 00:27:13.044
I knew I was cold, I knew I was hungry,
我明白我很冷，很饿

484
00:27:13.257 --> 00:27:15.498
but those things didn’t matter anymore.
但它们再也不起作用了

485
00:27:22.015 --> 00:27:27.260
I think we all have this idea of where our limits lie.
我认为我们都知道自己的极限在哪里

486
00:27:27.479 --> 00:27:28.969
If you’re hurting really bad,
如果你伤的特别狠

487
00:27:29.189 --> 00:27:31.976
you get to a point where you’re like, “I can’t endure any more.”
你就达到一个点，说，无法忍受更多了。

488
00:27:32.192 --> 00:27:35.309
And it takes something to force you past that.
于是它会推动你穿过去

489
00:27:36.905 --> 00:27:41.148
In Kyrgyzstan, I realized that my preconceived limits
在吉尔吉斯斯坦，我意识到自己曾经预想的极限

490
00:27:41.368 --> 00:27:43.825
were totally off base,
完全不靠谱

491
00:27:45.873 --> 00:27:47.488
that we’re capable of so much more
其实我们可以做到更多

492
00:27:47.708 --> 00:27:50.415
than we really could ever imagine.
比自己想象的多得多

493
00:27:56.091 --> 00:27:58.047
[Beth] There was this really hard climb nobody had done
有些很难的、没有人做到的攀岩

494
00:27:58.260 --> 00:28:00.717
that he tried the year before he cut off his finger,
他手指断以前，很早就尝试过

495
00:28:00.929 --> 00:28:02.590
and he couldn’t do it.
没有成功

496
00:28:02.806 --> 00:28:04.922
A year later, he came back without the finger
一年后，没了手指他再次回来

497
00:28:05.142 --> 00:28:06.848
and he did it.
却成功了

498
00:28:07.060 --> 00:28:08.891
[KeIIy] He cuts off his finger.
他切断了手指

499
00:28:09.104 --> 00:28:11.345
“Oh, no big deal. I’ll just get better after that.”
没啥大事，我会更好的

500
00:28:11.565 --> 00:28:13.977
I have no idea how that’s possible.
真不知道这是怎么做到的

501
00:28:16.069 --> 00:28:18.936
[Dad] That’s when Tommy took his game
这个，是Tommy想要完成他

502
00:28:19.156 --> 00:28:21.943
to the biggest stage on Earth, which is El Cap.
在地球最大舞台上的运动游戏，去攀登El Capitan


503
00:28:22.159 --> 00:28:23.444
[Long]At that time,
那时

504
00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:26.618
there were only a few free climbs that went up El Cap.
登上El Capitan 的徒手抱石攀岩只有几条线路

505
00:28:26.830 --> 00:28:29.742
[John] Some of the hardest big wall climbs ever done.
这些是人们完成过的最难的大岩体攀登

506
00:28:29.958 --> 00:28:31.949
Just to claim one of these routes
即使通过其中一条线路登顶

507
00:28:32.169 --> 00:28:35.081
would have been a monumental achievement
对于世界上最好的攀岩者来说

508
00:28:35.297 --> 00:28:37.458
for the best climbers in the world.
都可以说的不朽功绩

509
00:28:37.674 --> 00:28:39.710
And then Tommy walks into the Valley,
Tommy 于是来到这山谷

510
00:28:39.927 --> 00:28:42.293
missing a finger,
少一根手指

511
00:28:42.512 --> 00:28:45.754
and just started knocking them down, one after the other.
开始要一个一个击败它们

512
00:28:45.974 --> 00:28:49.512
[Long] Over the next five years, he went on a rampage.
此后的五年，他斗志昂扬

513
00:28:49.728 --> 00:28:52.185
[Tommy] I did basically all the existing routes on El Cap.
我完成了现有的全部登顶线路

514
00:28:52.397 --> 00:28:53.807
-Long]Salathe Wall 线路.
-[BethI The Zodiac 线路.

515
00:28:54.024 --> 00:28:55.013
[Dad] El Corazon 线路.

516
00:28:55.234 --> 00:28:56.349
-[Beth] Golden Gate 线路.
-[Dad] The Nose 线路.

517
00:28:56.568 --> 00:28:58.524
[John] Then he starts speed climbing these routes,
然后他开始高速攀登这些线路

518
00:28:58.737 --> 00:29:00.273
linking one into the other.
连接一些线路

519
00:29:00.489 --> 00:29:03.071
[Jason] Two El Cap routes in a day.
有时，一天之间，两次攀爬线路

520
00:29:03.283 --> 00:29:05.319
6,000 feet of climbing.
6000英尺的攀爬

521
00:29:05.535 --> 00:29:06.695
[Long] That was unheard of.
从未有人做到过

522
00:29:06.912 --> 00:29:08.903
-[Beth] You did it! 成功
-[Tommy] Oh, my goodness.天呐

523
00:29:09.122 --> 00:29:11.454
And then I started looking for new routes.
之后就想尝试新的线路

524
00:29:11.667 --> 00:29:15.034
[John] Tommy started looking between the lines
在线路之间，Tommy开始查看

525
00:29:15.254 --> 00:29:16.790
for his own first ascents.
找出他自己的第一条攀登线

526
00:29:17.005 --> 00:29:19.246
[Tommy]  It added that element of the unknown,
就是把未知加入进去

527
00:29:19.466 --> 00:29:22.674
this what-if, like, maybe that could be climbed.
嗯，也许，确实可以攀登

528
00:29:24.179 --> 00:29:26.215
[Long] I think Tommy had become hypnotized
我觉得Tommy是着迷了

529
00:29:26.431 --> 00:29:29.298
trying to figure out, where is the ultimate limit?
想要找出那条终极极线路

530
00:29:29.518 --> 00:29:31.008
[Brettl Oh, shit.哎，糟

531
00:29:32.646 --> 00:29:35.262
[Tommy] I did the first ascent of the Muir Wall.
我先试了Muir Wall 的第一条攀升线

532
00:29:35.482 --> 00:29:37.518
-[Beth] The West Buttress 线路.
-[KeIIy] Dihedral Wall线路.

533
00:29:37.734 --> 00:29:38.974
[Dad]Magic Mushroom.线路

534
00:29:39.194 --> 00:29:41.435
[Long] Anybody that does a first ascent on El Capitan
每一位成功完成El Capitan首次攀爬线路的人

535
00:29:41.655 --> 00:29:42.986
has their place in history forever.
都名垂千古

536
00:29:43.198 --> 00:29:45.439
Tommy did five of them.
Tommy完成了五条线路

537
00:29:45.659 --> 00:29:48.116
[Beth] Anything he could dream up, he did it.
每一个想到的梦想，他都要去实现

538
00:29:48.328 --> 00:29:51.491
And everyone in the climbing world is like, “What the hell?”
在攀岩界大家都感觉是深渊的

539
00:29:53.583 --> 00:29:54.868
[Long]He’s Mr. El Cap.
就是El Cap岩墙

540
00:29:55.085 --> 00:29:57.542
[John] The best big wall climber ever.
是攀岩者可能拥有的最棒大岩墙

541
00:29:59.506 --> 00:30:02.498
[Kelly] And Beth was with him all the time,
Beth一直和他在一起

542
00:30:02.718 --> 00:30:05.334
climbing all of these routes together.
一起攀爬这些线路

543
00:30:05.554 --> 00:30:07.260
[Beth] We just poured our hearts into climbing
我们把心都给予了攀登

544
00:30:07.472 --> 00:30:10.259
and supporting each other on these goals.
彼此支持去完成这些目标

545
00:30:10.475 --> 00:30:13.262
[Long] It was quite a team.
就是像一个团队

546
00:30:13.478 --> 00:30:15.969
[KeIIy] They were known as the first couple of climbing.
他们俩以攀登夫妻档著名

547
00:30:17.357 --> 00:30:19.643
There was one word Beth and Tommy.
就一个字：Beth 和Tommy

548
00:30:22.821 --> 00:30:24.277
[Tommy] We get married.
我们结婚了

549
00:30:24.489 --> 00:30:27.697
We ended up buying property like 20 minutes from El Capitan
我们到离开El Capitan 只有20分钟路程的地方买了地

550
00:30:27.909 --> 00:30:29.445
and building a house there.
建了一所房子

551
00:30:30.287 --> 00:30:31.743
We’re nearly there! 
几乎就在那里

552
00:30:31.955 --> 00:30:33.820
[Tommy] We were just going to live in Yosemite
我们要去优胜美地生活

553
00:30:34.041 --> 00:30:36.327
and raise our kids there and keep climbing.
生儿育女，继续攀登

554
00:30:36.543 --> 00:30:38.829
I was good friends with them both
我和他俩都是好友

555
00:30:39.046 --> 00:30:40.582
and we were next-door neighbors.
还是隔壁邻居

556
00:30:40.797 --> 00:30:42.162
They seemed so happy.
看起来他们那么快乐

557
00:30:42.382 --> 00:30:43.872
[Tommy] I’m like, wow, this life
我一直觉得，哇，这才是生活

558
00:30:44.092 --> 00:30:46.253
that I never even saw coming in the first place
我一直都没有想到会发生啥

559
00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:49.212
is starting to just magically appear.
只是等待奇迹自现

560
00:30:50.599 --> 00:30:54.387
Things are going seemingly really well,
看起来事事都好

561
00:30:54.603 --> 00:30:58.141
at least from my mind.
至少我心里是这么觉得的

562
00:30:58.357 --> 00:31:03.897
But I’m noticing, over time, little cracks started to form.
但，随着时间过去，我也注意到一些细小的裂痕

563
00:31:04.112 --> 00:31:07.195
The first inklings of almost hostility towards me.
最初对我的排斥迹象

564
00:31:08.450 --> 00:31:10.486
There was all this weird tension.
有一种奇怪的紧张

565
00:31:10.702 --> 00:31:11.908
And I was just like,
我当时觉得

566
00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:14.281
well, we’ve been together for eight years now.
在一起八年了

567
00:31:14.498 --> 00:31:16.284
Marriages go through troubling times.
婚姻都有艰难时刻

568
00:31:16.500 --> 00:31:22.370
We’ll get through this and just keep climbing.
我们会克服过去，继续攀岩的

569
00:31:22.589 --> 00:31:25.581
[Beth] I think there was a natural growing apart,
我想，这是一种自然而然的分离

570
00:31:25.801 --> 00:31:28.588
desires we had outside of climbing.
攀岩以外的驱动

571
00:31:30.389 --> 00:31:32.880
I think going through a super intense experience
我想通过经历一种超紧张状态

572
00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:34.965
like Kyrgyzstan...
比如像吉尔吉斯斯坦事件

573
00:31:36.311 --> 00:31:38.222
I mean, we were so young.
我意思是，我们都太年轻

574
00:31:38.438 --> 00:31:41.145
Years later, there’s probably a lot that started to come out,
多年以后，也许会发生更多

575
00:31:41.358 --> 00:31:42.848
healing that I hadn’t done.
我无法完成的心理愈合

576
00:31:43.068 --> 00:31:47.437
And at some point, the climbing we had
那时候

577
00:31:47.656 --> 00:31:51.194
wasn’t enough glue to hold it together anymore.
我们一起攀岩的状态也无法弥合彼此

578
00:31:51.410 --> 00:31:52.650
[Kelly] In Kyrgyzstan,
在吉尔吉斯斯坦

579
00:31:52.869 --> 00:31:56.612
Beth was extremely traumatized by those six days,
那六天的经历，对Beth的心理创伤很严重

580
00:31:56.832 --> 00:31:59.289
and Tommy was the person who saved them.
Tommy 救了他们

581
00:31:59.501 --> 00:32:01.207
And so from that, I think
从那个角度，我猜

582
00:32:01.420 --> 00:32:04.662
a sort of dependency probably developed
他们俩之间有可能有一种依赖

583
00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:09.591
that isn’t necessarily the same thing as true love.
并不等同于真爱

584
00:32:10.429 --> 00:32:11.635
[Tommy] Eventually,
最终结果是

585
00:32:11.847 --> 00:32:14.589
she started feeling something for somebody else.
她爱上了别人

586
00:32:15.851 --> 00:32:17.682
And...艾

587
00:32:19.521 --> 00:32:21.512
I don’t know how to summarize this.
不知道该怎么描述总结

588
00:32:21.731 --> 00:32:24.347
This is kind of a hard thing to talk about, but...
谈论这事真是很难，但

589
00:32:24.568 --> 00:32:27.605
that relationship with her and this other man just solidified
她和那个人的关系已经稳定

590
00:32:27.821 --> 00:32:29.812
in a way that she couldn’t walk away from that anymore.
她当时无法一走了之

591
00:32:30.031 --> 00:32:32.738
And she wanted that more than she wanted me.
比起需要我，她那时更需要他

592
00:32:36.705 --> 00:32:39.788
Once the divorce fully happened, I...
等离婚落定

593
00:32:42.252 --> 00:32:44.664
Yeah, I was just crushed.
是呀，当时我是崩溃的

594
00:32:46.465 --> 00:32:49.081
I drove to the rim of Yosemite Valley
我开车到优胜美地的山边

595
00:32:49.301 --> 00:32:51.963
and was looking across at El Capitan.
朝 El Capitan 望着

596
00:32:53.847 --> 00:32:57.260
It felt like El Cap was all I had.
好似 El Capitan 就是我的一切 

597
00:33:02.397 --> 00:33:03.728
Early in the morning,
清早

598
00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:07.182
there’s this one panel of the Wall that illuminates first.
岩墙上有一大片岩石会首先闪耀起来

599
00:33:14.284 --> 00:33:16.866
That’s why it’s called the Dawn Wall.
这是人们起名黎明墙的来由

600
00:33:19.831 --> 00:33:23.494
The last unclimbed big swath of stone.
最后一块人们从未攀爬过的大岩体

601
00:33:23.710 --> 00:33:25.792
I had looked at it a little bit before and knew
我看了好一会儿

602
00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:28.746
that it was way too hard, I’d never be able to do it.
知道这条路太难，我可能根本就完成不了

603
00:33:30.634 --> 00:33:32.374
But I was just hurting so bad
但在心灵受伤的那时刻

604
00:33:32.594 --> 00:33:34.255
that I had to figure out a distraction in life.
我必须找到生活的另一面

605
00:33:34.471 --> 00:33:38.009
I couldn’t just sit there and feel the pain.
不能一味坐着，经历悲伤

606
00:33:40.435 --> 00:33:43.302
I decided to go up there alone
我于是决定独自攀登

607
00:33:43.522 --> 00:33:47.140
and beat myself up on the Wall as just a way to cope.
用攀登黎明墙来战胜自我，作为面对生活的方式

608
00:33:52.072 --> 00:33:54.779
I walked around the back to the top of El Cap.
我从山后绕上 El Capitan 山顶

609
00:33:57.369 --> 00:33:59.985
I started rappelling down from above.
把绳索放下去

610
00:34:00.205 --> 00:34:03.618
And I put in a camp so I could stay up there.
架了一顶帐篷，然后可以呆在那儿

611
00:34:03.833 --> 00:34:06.119
And I started going through this process
探索

612
00:34:06.336 --> 00:34:10.079
of searching for a way to climb this section of the Wall.
可以攀爬这一部分大岩体的路

613
00:34:13.718 --> 00:34:16.551
The specific path was totally unknown.
具体的路径全然是未知的

614
00:34:18.598 --> 00:34:21.681
You look for weaknesses in the rock.
在岩石之中找出薄弱点

615
00:34:21.893 --> 00:34:24.851
Corners that you can wedge your body into.
那些可以把身体楔入的石头角落

616
00:34:25.063 --> 00:34:27.554
Cracks for your hands and toes.
可以放住手足的缝隙

617
00:34:27.774 --> 00:34:30.311
Little edges for your fingertips.
手指可以扒住的点滴岩石边缘

618
00:34:30.527 --> 00:34:32.518
Anything that you could possibly grab onto
任何可以抓牢的部位

619
00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:35.194
that would make this wall climbable.
这样才有爬上去的可能

620
00:34:39.744 --> 00:34:41.951
At first, it was just hanging on the rope,
开始时，挂在绳索上

621
00:34:43.582 --> 00:34:45.243
analyzing the surface of the rock
分析岩石表面

622
00:34:45.458 --> 00:34:47.414
to see if there was holds.
查看可以抓住的地方

623
00:34:51.923 --> 00:34:54.255
Just finding something to obsess about
好似拼命找到沉迷的事物

624
00:34:54.467 --> 00:34:57.834
so I wouldn’t obsess about my divorce.
避免落入离婚的困局

625
00:34:58.054 --> 00:35:00.261
[Kelly] I think it’s probably important
我认为这事很重要

626
00:35:00.473 --> 00:35:03.681
that it was an impossible level of rock climbing.
因为这是一种几乎不可能发生的攀岩

627
00:35:03.893 --> 00:35:07.511
When you absorb yourself in some magnificent challenge,
当你沉浸在某种崇高的挑战中

628
00:35:07.731 --> 00:35:10.564
there is no space to be thinking about anything else.
就没有心思去考虑其它了

629
00:35:14.070 --> 00:35:15.685
You know, if you’re heartbroken,
你懂的，在心碎时刻

630
00:35:15.905 --> 00:35:19.944
just throw yourself into an impossible wall.
把自己投身到一堵不可完成的岩墙

631
00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:22.151
[Tommy] So I was sitting up there through this storm.
因此那时，我面临内心的暴风骤雨，枯坐着

632
00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:24.201
My wife has left me.
老婆离开了

633
00:35:24.414 --> 00:35:26.575
She was the only person I had climbed with
她是我攀爬的唯一同行

634
00:35:26.791 --> 00:35:29.407
for, like, ten years.
有十年之久

635
00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:32.706
In my portaledge at night,
那一夜，在悬吊帐篷里

636
00:35:32.922 --> 00:35:35.379
weeping and really feeling sorry for myself,
泪奔，自怨自怜

637
00:35:35.592 --> 00:35:37.628
trying to find this elusive thing
企图找到逃避的路

638
00:35:37.844 --> 00:35:39.550
that probably didn’t even exist.
也许根本就不存在

639
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.425
[Dad] I was concerned.
我关注到

640
00:35:43.642 --> 00:35:45.803
He just seemed to be suffering at that point.
他那时内心受伤很重

641
00:35:46.019 --> 00:35:48.055
And I wanted to see what this was all about,
我也想这是怎么了

642
00:35:48.271 --> 00:35:51.729
so early on in the game I went up there with him.
所以我上去和他一起

643
00:35:51.941 --> 00:35:54.978
[Tommy] I convinced my dad to come up there and belay me,
我说服我老爹上来，帮我放安全绳

644
00:35:55.195 --> 00:36:00.064
so I could start actually trying to climb sections of the route.
这样我就能真正探索攀登的线路

645
00:36:01.576 --> 00:36:04.488
-[Groans] -What the heck?
怎么啦？

646
00:36:04.704 --> 00:36:07.286
[Dad] I really had my doubts as to whether it was going to be
我真是很疑惑

647
00:36:07.499 --> 00:36:09.285
a viable climb.
这是不是可行的攀爬

648
00:36:09.501 --> 00:36:10.661
-[Dad]Be safe. 保持安全
-[Tommy]I will. 会的

649
00:36:10.877 --> 00:36:12.538
-[Dad] Get strong. 挺住
-[Tommy] Yup. 会的

650
00:36:12.754 --> 00:36:14.665
But during that period of time,
就在那段时间

651
00:36:14.881 --> 00:36:18.089
he became convinced that it was somehow possible.
他开始相信，也许是可行的

652
00:36:20.303 --> 00:36:22.339
[Long] Tommy spent an entire year
Tommy花了整整一年功夫

653
00:36:22.555 --> 00:36:26.218
swinging around looking for a route up the Dawn Wall,
晃动在岩石上，寻求黎明墙的登顶途径

654
00:36:28.728 --> 00:36:30.434
trying to connect the dots
尝试把零落的攀爬岩点连接起来

655
00:36:30.647 --> 00:36:32.888
from the bottom all the way to the top
从最底部一直到山顶

656
00:36:33.108 --> 00:36:37.351
so you can someday hope to free climb the whole thing.
梦想有一天，终究可以做到徒手抱石攀登整个黎明墙。

657
00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:39.936
[Tommy]  Eventually, I found a route
最后，我找到了一条路

658
00:36:40.156 --> 00:36:43.444
that seemed like it was theoretically possible,
一条理论上可行的线路

659
00:36:43.660 --> 00:36:45.867
like I found the path through the maze maybe.
好比在迷宫里找到一条出路

660
00:36:46.746 --> 00:36:48.111
But I realized
但我意识到

661
00:36:48.331 --> 00:36:50.947
there was no way I was going to be able to do this alone.
我绝不可能独自一人完成

662
00:36:51.167 --> 00:36:55.160
It’s just a monumental project.
这是一个具有纪念意义的计划

663
00:36:55.380 --> 00:36:59.089
Without Beth, I needed to find a partner,
失去了Beth，我需要找一个同伴

664
00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:03.626
somebody that I could rely on
一个可以信赖

665
00:37:04.931 --> 00:37:06.887
to help me solve this puzzle.
帮助我解决疑惑的同伴

666
00:37:17.986 --> 00:37:20.477
[Wind blowingl

667
00:37:32.208 --> 00:37:35.166
[Tommy] I should wake Kevin up with some coffee.
我要用咖啡叫醒Kevin

668
00:37:38.465 --> 00:37:40.001
Just stretching.
抻一抻

669
00:37:40.216 --> 00:37:42.002
[Tommy] That’s a good idea.
好办法

670
00:37:42.218 --> 00:37:44.550
I felt a little rugged when I first woke up.
我觉得一醒来时有点糟

671
00:37:44.763 --> 00:37:45.878
But how are you feeling?
你感觉如何？

672
00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:48.258
Still stuffy and sore throat. Kind of achy.
有点闷闷的，嗓子疼。别处也疼

673
00:37:48.475 --> 00:37:51.262
[Tommy] I think I got whatever you got.
我觉得和你差不多

674
00:37:56.816 --> 00:37:59.558
[Long] After the first couple of days on the Wall,
在岩壁上的头几天

675
00:37:59.778 --> 00:38:02.110
there’s a small little cadre of people down in the meadow
山下的草坪上聚集了一些人

676
00:38:02.322 --> 00:38:04.313
following their progress.
观望他们的进展

677
00:38:04.532 --> 00:38:06.614
You can get a telescope or a pair of binoculars,
你可以拿一架（天文）望远镜或双筒望远镜

678
00:38:06.826 --> 00:38:08.441
look up at this spectacle happening.
观看这个奇迹

679
00:38:08.661 --> 00:38:09.992
Oh, my God.
老天

680
00:38:10.205 --> 00:38:12.912
-Is he naked or what? 他光着身子吗？
-[Laughing] 哈哈哈

681
00:38:14.292 --> 00:38:15.828
[Tom]My name is Tom Evans. I’ve been
我是Tom Evans

682
00:38:16.044 --> 00:38:18.456
for many years photographing climbers on El Cap.
我已经花好几年拍摄攀登El Cap岩体的人 

683
00:38:18.671 --> 00:38:20.332
I usually don’t come in the winter,
一般我不在冬天来

684
00:38:20.548 --> 00:38:22.630
but this is big news in climbing.
在这次是登山界的大新闻

685
00:38:22.842 --> 00:38:24.833
And we’ve all been pulling for him for many years.
我们被他吸引了好多年

686
00:38:25.053 --> 00:38:26.543
[Matt] I was on a little vacation from work,
当时我正在休假中

687
00:38:26.763 --> 00:38:28.503
and I decided to come out from Sacramento
决定从萨克拉门托 （Sacramento） 过来

688
00:38:28.723 --> 00:38:31.055
to watch these guys climb the Dawn Wall.
来观看他们攀登黎明墙

689
00:38:31.267 --> 00:38:33.223
It’s definitely a moment in history.
绝对是历史一刻

690
00:38:33.436 --> 00:38:35.347
To be able to be a part of that and witness it
参与并目睹

691
00:38:35.563 --> 00:38:36.894
is pretty phenomenal.
特别值

692
00:38:39.859 --> 00:38:42.271
[Tommy] Pushing forward.
推进

693
00:38:42.487 --> 00:38:46.947
From here on up, every pitch is pretty legit.
从现在开始，每一绳距都很规范

694
00:38:48.910 --> 00:38:51.276
We’ve got to pace ourselves.
我们需要调整步调

695
00:38:51.496 --> 00:38:53.782
Maybe one or two pitches a day.
大概每天一两个绳距

696
00:38:54.833 --> 00:38:56.494
[Kevin] Come on, Tommy.
加油，Tommy

697
00:38:59.546 --> 00:39:01.207
Good.好

698
00:39:01.422 --> 00:39:02.707
Good, Tommy. Come on.
好哒，Tommy， 加油

699
00:39:05.260 --> 00:39:06.340
[Brett] Nice.
挺棒

700
00:39:07.053 --> 00:39:08.042
[Tommy]Yeah. 是

701
00:39:12.934 --> 00:39:14.265
Come on. 加油

702
00:39:14.477 --> 00:39:15.967
You got it.
成了。

703
00:39:16.187 --> 00:39:17.802
Yeah. Yeah, Kevin.
对对对，Kevin

704
00:39:18.022 --> 00:39:20.479
Nice, dude.
赞一个，哥们

705
00:39:20.692 --> 00:39:22.683
-[Kevin] Cool.
-[Tommy] Dude, that was sick.
哎，糟

706
00:39:22.902 --> 00:39:27.191
It’s day three on the Wall, and we sent pitch 10.
登山第三天。我们到了第十绳距

707
00:39:27.949 --> 00:39:29.189
Yeah! 耶

708
00:39:29.409 --> 00:39:30.990
Yeah. Boom. 耶，好耶

709
00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:33.113
-Things are going good.
-Things are going good.
进展不错

710
00:39:34.873 --> 00:39:36.784
[Kevin] And the forecast is calling
天气预报说

711
00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:39.412
for super cold windy temps tomorrow,
明天是超级寒冷大风天

712
00:39:39.627 --> 00:39:41.288
so we’re going to rest.
我们准备休整

713
00:39:43.464 --> 00:39:45.750
[Tommy] Urgent weather message.
紧急天气信息

714
00:39:45.967 --> 00:39:49.755
Winds, 50 miles per hour with gusts 75 or higher.
风速，每小时50英里，阵风的时速是75或更高

715
00:39:49.971 --> 00:39:53.134
Impact... downed trees, downed power lines,
影响：倒下的树木，倒下的电力线

716
00:39:53.349 --> 00:39:55.214
flying portaledges.
乱晃的悬空帐篷

717
00:39:58.771 --> 00:40:00.853
[Long] These guys are up there in the middle of winter,
这俩哥们在大冬天里挂在空中

718
00:40:01.065 --> 00:40:02.726
which is almost unheard of.
闻所未闻

719
00:40:02.942 --> 00:40:04.933
But they need it to be as cold as possible
但他们需要寒冷

720
00:40:05.153 --> 00:40:07.860
so they can stick to the tiny holds
因此才能抠进细小的石缝

721
00:40:08.072 --> 00:40:09.983
There’s nobody else on the Wall.
岩壁上没有别的人

722
00:40:10.199 --> 00:40:13.862
Last night, the temperature dropped 30 degrees.
头一个晚上，气温下降了30度

723
00:40:14.078 --> 00:40:16.285
To be up there under these conditions,
在这种情形下呆在岩壁上

724
00:40:16.497 --> 00:40:19.284
it’s horrendous. I don’t know how they do it.
真是可怕。不知道他们是怎样做到的

725
00:40:23.254 --> 00:40:24.710
Carabiners, locked
钩环铁锁，扣好

726
00:40:24.923 --> 00:40:28.131
The windchill’s like negative 20 or something.
寒风指数差不多是零下20度或更低

727
00:40:28.343 --> 00:40:30.083
How you feeling over there, KJ?
Kevin J 你觉得怎样？

728
00:40:33.139 --> 00:40:35.050
It’s getting pretty rowdy.
已经可以用粗暴来形容啦

729
00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:37.973
[Kevin] On El Cap, the wind blows straight up the wall.
在El Cap，风是直接吹到岩壁上去的

730
00:40:38.186 --> 00:40:41.303
The ledge would float up and, bang, back into the wall.
岩石凸都快被吹飞了，砰，风再砸向岩壁

731
00:40:44.776 --> 00:40:46.858
Oh, boy. 哥们，天哪

732
00:40:47.070 --> 00:40:50.312
[Brett] Tommy feels right at home.
Tommy 就像呆在家里一样

733
00:40:50.531 --> 00:40:53.068
Argh![Laughing]
啊哈哈哈

734
00:40:54.994 --> 00:40:56.609
[Tommy] I don’t know what’s wrong with me,
我都不知道我怎么了

735
00:40:56.829 --> 00:40:58.535
but I love this shit.
不过我真喜欢这天气

736
00:41:02.085 --> 00:41:05.452
[Brett] It might be smart to stay in the ledges today.
今天呆在岩架上是很明智的

737
00:41:07.048 --> 00:41:11.417
[Kevin] Because of the windstorm the day before,
因为，前一天的大风暴

738
00:41:11.636 --> 00:41:13.718
all of this moisture froze,
都上冻了

739
00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:17.138
like salt on a Margarita glass on the top of El Cap.
El Cap的岩顶，就像玛格丽塔玻璃杯中的盐

740
00:41:17.350 --> 00:41:20.262
And as soon as the sun hit the top of the Wall,
等太阳光线照到岩峰顶端

741
00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:26.895
that ice just started to shower down on top of us.
冰块就纷至沓来，倾倒到我们头顶

742
00:41:31.781 --> 00:41:34.363
These missiles flying by our camp.
导弹般飞临到我们营地

743
00:41:34.575 --> 00:41:37.408
You hear it before you see it.
还没有看见之前，就能先听到它们

744
00:41:37.620 --> 00:41:40.407
I’m like, this is a deadly situation.
我在想，这也太操蛋了吧

745
00:41:42.417 --> 00:41:44.783
-[Kevin]That was fucked up.
-[Brett]Did you get hit?
简直糟透了 ----- 你被砸到了没？

746
00:41:45.003 --> 00:41:46.789
[Kevin]No, but that was just pure luck.
没，纯粹运气好

747
00:41:48.464 --> 00:41:49.419
[Brett] That was scary.
这真是骇人

748
00:41:49.632 --> 00:41:51.122
[Kevin] I hate that shit.
我恨死这鬼天气了

749
00:41:51.342 --> 00:41:54.379
[Brett]Here come some more big chunks. Tommy forgot his helmet.
大头神经了，Tommy忘记带岩盔

750
00:41:54.595 --> 00:41:56.460
[Kevin] Heads up, Tommy.
看头，Tommy

751
00:41:58.349 --> 00:42:01.682
[Brett]Tommy doesn’t seem too concerned. What the fuck?
Tommy居然不在意。没岩盔又怎么啦

752
00:42:01.894 --> 00:42:03.475
[Kevin] What’s new?
没事吧？
 
753
00:42:03.688 --> 00:42:06.896
Tommy, he was made for something like this.
Tommy，他就像为此而生

754
00:42:07.108 --> 00:42:12.648
But for me, it took a long time to get comfortable on the Wall.
不过对于我，花了好一段时间才习惯自如

755
00:42:12.864 --> 00:42:15.526
[Long] You can understand, Tommy grew up in the mountains.
你可以理解为，因为Tommy就在山里长大

756
00:42:15.742 --> 00:42:18.279
He’d spent the better part of his adult life
他成年后很大一部分生活

757
00:42:18.494 --> 00:42:21.281
on El Capitan trying to do free climbs.
都是在El Capitan，想要徒手抱石攀爬

758
00:42:21.497 --> 00:42:25.661
But this guy Kevin was raised in Santa Rosa. I think.
但，据我了解，Kevin老弟是在Santa Rosa 长大的

759
00:42:25.877 --> 00:42:28.368
You know, wine country.
你知道吧，就是在葡萄园的地盘上长大的

760
00:42:28.588 --> 00:42:31.830
[kevin] There’s not a lot of rock climbing in Santa Rosa.
Santa Rosa 可是木有多少攀岩的地方

761
00:42:32.050 --> 00:42:34.257
-[Eric]First ascent.第一攀
-[Kevin] Yeah! 耶

762
00:42:34.469 --> 00:42:37.461
[Eric] Don’t fall on the Camaro.
别在Camaro 掉下来喔

763
00:42:37.680 --> 00:42:41.969
[Kevin] I found climbing through the local gym.
我是在当地体育馆里发掘到攀岩的

764
00:42:42.185 --> 00:42:44.267
-[Gail] Bye, honey. Have fun. 儿子再见，好好玩吧
-[Kevin] Bye, Mom. 老妈再见

765
00:42:44.479 --> 00:42:45.810
[Eric] Drive careful.好好开车啦

766
00:42:46.022 --> 00:42:47.978
[Kevin] I got really into this particular form of climbing
我实在是被这种特别的攀岩所吸引

767
00:42:48.191 --> 00:42:50.022
called bouldering.
就是抱石攀岩

768
00:42:50.234 --> 00:42:53.226
It’s typically 30 feet or less.
通常（一个典型的绳距）是30英尺左右

769
00:42:53.446 --> 00:42:55.858
Doesn’t require any gear.
没有其它器械的辅助

770
00:42:56.074 --> 00:42:58.565
Bouldering’s just about athieticism
抱石攀岩具有竞技精神

771
00:42:58.785 --> 00:43:01.026
and difficulty in its purest form.
它纯粹的难度也是魅力

772
00:43:04.457 --> 00:43:05.697
[Long] Bouldering is all about
抱石攀岩

773
00:43:05.917 --> 00:43:08.249
trying the hardest individual moves.
完全是在尝试个人运动中最难的动作

774
00:43:08.461 --> 00:43:09.576
[Groans]

775
00:43:11.005 --> 00:43:14.418
And Kevin quickly became very, very talented.
Kevin很快就证明了自己的天赋

776
00:43:15.593 --> 00:43:17.675
He was one of the best in the world.
他变成世界顶尖之一

777
00:43:20.264 --> 00:43:22.676
But only up to about 30 feet.
但也仅仅，就是上升了30英尺

778
00:43:24.519 --> 00:43:28.307
[Kevin] In 2009, I was at the top of my game in bouldering
2009年，我当时在抱石攀岩的顶峰时期

779
00:43:29.524 --> 00:43:32.106
and looking for something new.
想尝试一点新的

780
00:43:34.403 --> 00:43:37.987
I kept hearing about this futuristic thing
就不断听到这个即将发生的事

781
00:43:38.199 --> 00:43:40.190
that Tommy was working on.
有关Tommy在做的事

782
00:43:40.409 --> 00:43:42.525
I had zero big wall experience.
对于大岩墙攀岩，我是零经验

783
00:43:42.745 --> 00:43:44.406
Tommy and I didn’t know each other at all.
和 Tommy 也根本不认识

784
00:43:44.622 --> 00:43:46.863
But I just sent him a message out of the blue.
莫名其妙地，我就发了一条信息给他

785
00:43:47.083 --> 00:43:48.619
“Hey, do you need a partner?”
嗨，你要不要一个搭档？

786
00:43:48.835 --> 00:43:52.327
And to my utter shock, he said, meet me in Yosemite in October.
出乎我意料，他说，那么，十月我们在优胜美地见面

787
00:43:53.798 --> 00:43:55.709
[Tommy] I knew Kevin by reputation.
我早听说过Kevin

788
00:43:55.925 --> 00:43:58.462
He was this amazingly strong bouldering kid.
他是个特别出色的抱石攀岩小孩

789
00:43:58.678 --> 00:44:00.293
And I thought to myself,“What the heck?
我对自己说，担心啥呢？

790
00:44:00.513 --> 00:44:02.674
“Maybe he could be an asset.”
说不定他正好就是那个真正搭档

791
00:44:02.890 --> 00:44:04.755
Plus, he was the only one interested.
此外，他也是唯一有兴趣的那个

792
00:44:04.976 --> 00:44:07.558
Everybody else thought I was crazy.
其他人都觉得我不可理喻

793
00:44:09.480 --> 00:44:10.435
[Kevin] Show up.
来吧

794
00:44:10.648 --> 00:44:12.354
I remember standing there with Tommy,
我还记得很清楚

795
00:44:12.567 --> 00:44:14.023
who’s a legend figure in my life.
当时和Tommy站一起，他可是我的传奇英雄呢

796
00:44:14.235 --> 00:44:16.772
I feel like such a fucking dork.
我觉得自己特傻

797
00:44:16.988 --> 00:44:19.149
Who am I? I’ve never climbed El Cap.
我是谁呀？从未攀登过El Cap 

798
00:44:19.365 --> 00:44:20.775
What a noob.
纯粹一菜鸟

799
00:44:20.992 --> 00:44:22.152
Fiddling around on boulders,
就是在抱石这事上扯蛋

800
00:44:22.368 --> 00:44:24.324
that’s a far cry from being on El Capitan.
和登上El Cap 全不是一回事

801
00:44:24.537 --> 00:44:27.324
[Tommy] First thing I had to do was test him.
我要做的第一件事就是测试

802
00:44:28.583 --> 00:44:30.699
I gave him like an 80 pound haul bag.
我给了他一个80磅的拖袋

803
00:44:30.918 --> 00:44:32.624
[Kevin] A soul crushing load.
真是沉死人的东西

804
00:44:32.837 --> 00:44:34.418
[Tommy] We hiked to the top of El Cap.
我们徒步到达El Cap峰顶

805
00:44:34.630 --> 00:44:36.291
[Kevin]
We spent the night on top.
就在那里露天度过一个晚上

806
00:44:36.507 --> 00:44:38.043
Woke up early the next day...
第二天醒来时

807
00:44:38.259 --> 00:44:40.420
[Tommy] It’s 3:15 in the morning.
是凌晨3:15

808
00:44:40.636 --> 00:44:41.921
Cooking up a little breakfast.
煮了一点早饭

809
00:44:42.138 --> 00:44:44.299
You never get up at 3:00 in the morning to go bouldering.
你永远也不会凌晨3点去抱石攀岩的

810
00:44:45.808 --> 00:44:48.515
[Kevin]...and start rappelling down the face.
然后开始沿绳索下到岩石表层

811
00:44:51.731 --> 00:44:54.689
You start walking backwards.
开始回走

812
00:44:54.901 --> 00:44:57.893
It’s like stepping off the edge of the Earth.
这几乎像从地球的边缘跨出去

813
00:45:06.078 --> 00:45:09.696
You instantly have 3,000 feet of exposure under your butt.
屁股底下，是3000英尺高的野外

814
00:45:09.916 --> 00:45:12.578
[Howling, laughing]

815
00:45:12.793 --> 00:45:14.158
Oh, my God! 天呐

816
00:45:16.547 --> 00:45:18.128
[Tommy] How’s it going up there, Key?
Key，感觉如何？

817
00:45:18.341 --> 00:45:20.297
-[Kevin]Good, I got the bag. 不错，我还有一个包
-[Tommy]And my shoes? 我鞋子在吗？

818
00:45:20.509 --> 00:45:23.922
-[Kevin]And your shoes. 是，还有你鞋子
-[Tommy]Cool, thank you. 酷，谢啦

819
00:45:24.138 --> 00:45:26.845
It’s scary to be a total beginner again.
再次成为新手，这一点挺吓人的

820
00:45:27.058 --> 00:45:28.764
I don’t know any of this stuff.
我对此（这种攀岩）一无所知

821
00:45:30.144 --> 00:45:33.352
Trying to figure out how to jumar a fixed line.
要弄明白怎样用固定绳索上升器

822
00:45:33.564 --> 00:45:35.475
[Groans]

823
00:45:35.691 --> 00:45:37.727
How to set up a portaledge.
如何搭建悬空帐篷

824
00:45:39.362 --> 00:45:41.227
[Clanging]

825
00:45:45.660 --> 00:45:46.900
Sorry, Kevin.抱歉，Kevin

826
00:45:47.119 --> 00:45:50.407
[Kevin] I’ll just hold this quarter in. It’s cool.
我正抓着咱的营帐进来了，超酷

827
00:45:50.623 --> 00:45:53.706
How to take a dump on the side of the Wall.
怎样在岩壁上扔垃圾

828
00:45:53.918 --> 00:45:56.409
-[Tommy] They get every moment. 他们一直在拍摄你呢
-[Josh] Close up. 别说了


829
00:45:59.340 --> 00:46:03.925
[Kevin]At this point, I have no idea what I’m getting into,
直到那会儿，我还是对参与的这件事比较无知

830
00:46:04.136 --> 00:46:07.503
no idea that it’s about to consume six years of my life.
不知道会消耗我六年的时间

831
00:46:08.975 --> 00:46:11.432
[Kelly] When Kevin joined on with Tommy,
当Kevin加入到Tommy一起

832
00:46:13.271 --> 00:46:15.512
it was the first time since getting divorced
这是Tommy离婚后的第一次

833
00:46:15.731 --> 00:46:17.767
that Tommy had a partner.
有了搭档

834
00:46:19.235 --> 00:46:20.975
There’s two bolts and then an old bolt.
有两个螺栓，还有一个旧螺栓

835
00:46:21.195 --> 00:46:24.733
[Kevin]I didn’t know what we were up against,
我并不知道我们面临的是什么

836
00:46:24.949 --> 00:46:28.362
but I was going on faith that this is Tommy’s world.
但我相信这是Tommy的世界

837
00:46:28.577 --> 00:46:32.115
He’s got the clear vision of what this could be.
他对所作所为一清二楚

838
00:46:32.331 --> 00:46:34.617
And I’m just going to trust that.
我只需要信任它就好

839
00:46:37.461 --> 00:46:38.997
[Tommy] The basic strategy early on
最开始的计划

840
00:46:39.213 --> 00:46:41.124
was not to climb the route from the bottom.
并不是从岩底攀登

841
00:46:41.340 --> 00:46:43.706
It was to identify the hardest sections
无疑这是最难的部分

842
00:46:43.926 --> 00:46:45.462
and focus on those first.
把注意力集中在这里

843
00:46:45.678 --> 00:46:47.919
[Kevin]There were all these question marks.
所有的问号都在这儿

844
00:46:48.139 --> 00:46:49.720
Come on, Tommy. 加油，Tommy

845
00:46:49.932 --> 00:46:51.468
[Tommy] OK, take it there. 好吧，拿上去

846
00:46:51.684 --> 00:46:54.016
Oh, I got the pinch with my right hand instead of my left.
我用右手标记了，没有用左手

847
00:46:54.228 --> 00:46:55.434
[Kevin] Working it out. 完成它

848
00:46:55.646 --> 00:46:57.102
Constantly working it out.不断完成

849
00:46:58.691 --> 00:47:01.979
Early on, most of it was figuring out what didn’t work.
起先，大部分计划都是在琢磨难以完成的部分

850
00:47:08.034 --> 00:47:09.365
Right in the middle of the Wall,
在岩壁的中部

851
00:47:09.577 --> 00:47:11.613
we were gonna have to traverse it sideways.
我们必须窄道横穿

852
00:47:11.829 --> 00:47:13.410
Come on.加油

853
00:47:16.876 --> 00:47:18.662
Come on.加油

854
00:47:18.878 --> 00:47:20.493
I don’t see any holds,
我简直什么抓缝也看不到

855
00:47:20.713 --> 00:47:23.796
but I try to harness some of Tommy’s optimism.
不过我控制自己学习Tommy的乐观

856
00:47:26.093 --> 00:47:27.378
[Tommy] After the traverse,
在横穿以后

857
00:47:27.595 --> 00:47:30.462
there’s this 8 and 112 foot blank section.
紧接著就是8到112英寸的空白地带

858
00:47:30.681 --> 00:47:32.046
Completely smooth.
完全是光溜溜的岩壁

859
00:47:32.266 --> 00:47:35.099
Nothing that you could even get your fingernails behind.
没有任何可以手指触碰的地方

860
00:47:35.311 --> 00:47:37.302
The only way was to just leap.
唯一的办法就是跳跃

861
00:47:38.981 --> 00:47:40.937
This crazy dynamic move.
真是疯狂的动作

862
00:47:41.150 --> 00:47:42.265
The Dyno.在Dyno段

863
00:47:42.485 --> 00:47:43.975
I didn’t really believe it would be possible
我真不敢相信这怎么可能呢

864
00:47:44.195 --> 00:47:45.480
until I saw Kevin try it.
直到看见Kevin在尝试

865
00:47:47.823 --> 00:47:49.563
Yeah, man. It was close.
兄弟，接近了

866
00:47:49.784 --> 00:47:51.445
He showed me that it was.
他展示给我

867
00:47:51.660 --> 00:47:54.447
[Kevin] Come on. All you got.
加油，快了

868
00:47:54.663 --> 00:47:57.200
Above the Dyno, you have pitch after pitch
Dyno段之上，每一个绳距

869
00:47:57.416 --> 00:47:58.952
of have super smooth granite,
都是光滑无比的花岗岩

870
00:47:59.168 --> 00:48:00.829
extremely polished.
呈极端抛光状

871
00:48:02.088 --> 00:48:04.079
Because of Tommy’s missing index finger,
因为Tommy没有了食指

872
00:48:04.298 --> 00:48:07.461
he’s using his thumbs in crazy ways.
他很不可思议地用拇指替代

873
00:48:11.806 --> 00:48:13.296
Shit.狗屎

874
00:48:13.516 --> 00:48:15.302
Argh! 啊

875
00:48:16.477 --> 00:48:18.308
Holy crap, that is hard.
艾玛，真是太难了

876
00:48:18.521 --> 00:48:21.388
13B.

877
00:48:21.607 --> 00:48:23.643
13C. 14A.

878
00:48:23.859 --> 00:48:26.726
[Long] To understand the difficulty of this route,
想要理解这段路径的困难度

879
00:48:26.946 --> 00:48:31.315
you have to understand climbing grades.
你不得不要先理解攀岩等级

880
00:48:31.534 --> 00:48:33.399
Climbers use a numerical system
攀岩者是使用一套数值系统

881
00:48:33.619 --> 00:48:35.826
to rate the difficulty of each pitch.
来评估每一个绳距的难度系数

882
00:48:36.038 --> 00:48:38.700
The higher the number, the harder the pitch.
系数越高，绳距难度越大

883
00:48:38.916 --> 00:48:41.953
Once you get into 513 and 514 level,
一旦到达513和514的难度系数

884
00:48:42.169 --> 00:48:43.909
that’s virtuoso territory.
那是大师级的恐怖系数了

885
00:48:45.881 --> 00:48:47.997
The Dawn Wall has more hard pitches
黎明墙的绳距难度系数

886
00:48:48.217 --> 00:48:51.801
than every other route on El Cap combined.
比所有El Cap岩墙的难度系数都要更高

887
00:49:00.146 --> 00:49:01.431
I always thought it was futile
我总是认为

888
00:49:01.647 --> 00:49:03.308
in terms of doing the whole thing.
要完成整个攀登几乎是徒劳

889
00:49:05.276 --> 00:49:08.393
This is a pipe dream, man. Come on.
哥们，这是梦想啊，加油

890
00:49:08.612 --> 00:49:11.319
[Kevin] The next few years were a grind.
此后的几年真是很磨人

891
00:49:11.532 --> 00:49:16.652
Coming back every spring and every fall for months at a time.
每个春秋时季，都会回来呆上几个月

892
00:49:19.832 --> 00:49:22.494
-[Tommy] Come on. 加油
-[Thunderclap]

893
00:49:23.961 --> 00:49:27.374
[Kevin] Living on the Wall takes a huge toll.
住了岩壁上是要付出代价的

894
00:49:27.590 --> 00:49:29.797
[Tommy] This is what El Cap does to your feet.
这是 El Cap 对你脚丫子的所作所为 

895
00:49:30.009 --> 00:49:31.965
[Kevin] We’d stay up there a few days...
我们要呆好几天.......

896
00:49:32.178 --> 00:49:34.669
[Brett] Oh, my God. That’s a lot of air time.
天呐，真是飞天了

897
00:49:35.890 --> 00:49:38.381
[Kevin]...go down, rest,
下来，休息

898
00:49:38.601 --> 00:49:39.636
try again.
再尝试

899
00:49:39.852 --> 00:49:42.594
There were always new problems to face.
不断有新问题出现

900
00:49:42.813 --> 00:49:43.928
[Tommy] Get out of here!
快撤出来

901
00:49:46.484 --> 00:49:48.190
Come on, Kevin. Do it, man.
加油，Kevin，你行的，兄弟

902
00:49:50.446 --> 00:49:51.856
-Really close. 几乎抓到了
-Oh, I sprained my ankle. 我伤到了脚踝

903
00:49:52.072 --> 00:49:53.608
-Are you OK, man? 怎么样，兄弟
-Oh, shit. 糟透了

904
00:49:53.824 --> 00:49:56.065
[Kevin]So many reasons to give up.
N多可以放弃的理由

905
00:49:57.703 --> 00:49:59.034
[Brett] Oh, shit. 啊，糟了

906
00:49:59.246 --> 00:50:02.454
[Tommy] Man, I think I have broke or dislocated ribs.
兄弟，我觉得我胸骨折断了，要不就是错位了。

907
00:50:02.666 --> 00:50:04.031
We’re heading to the clinic.
我们跑医疗室

908
00:50:04.251 --> 00:50:05.582
Maybe they’ll just pop it back in.
也许他们可以设法弄好

909
00:50:05.794 --> 00:50:08.251
[Kevin]They will, and we’ll go back up later tonight.
他们会，哎，我们会晚上再过来

910
00:50:09.256 --> 00:50:11.338
But Tommy was committed.
但是，Tommy决意已定

911
00:50:13.052 --> 00:50:14.792
[Tommy] Come on, Kevin! Come on!
加油，Kevin，加油

912
00:50:15.012 --> 00:50:17.344
[Kevin]There were times I thought he was totally crazy.
我不由自主有时想，他真是疯了

913
00:50:17.556 --> 00:50:19.342
Come on! 加油

914
00:50:21.727 --> 00:50:23.058
Yee-hoo! 呼呼

915
00:50:23.270 --> 00:50:26.103
Whoo! Ow-ow! 哇塞

916
00:50:30.486 --> 00:50:32.977
[Kevin]When we weren’t together on the Wall,
当我们不在岩墙时 

917
00:50:33.197 --> 00:50:35.313
we would go home to our own worlds,
我们就回到自己的世界

918
00:50:36.700 --> 00:50:38.782
check in on loved ones.
和亲爱的家人照个面

919
00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:44.072
It’s gross. I can see the oil on your hair.
油腻腻的，我都看见你头发上的油了

920
00:50:45.709 --> 00:50:48.075
OK, I’m just totally being a mom.
好吧，我就是个老妈的命

921
00:50:50.297 --> 00:50:52.663
[kevin]
Try to get some good rest
要好好休息哦

922
00:50:52.883 --> 00:50:57.092
and find motivation for the next round of attempts.
充电了才好继续尝试

923
00:51:01.141 --> 00:51:02.472
[Tommy] When I wasn’t on the Dawn Wall,
我不在黎明墙时

924
00:51:02.685 --> 00:51:05.802
I was living by myself in Colorado,
我就独自住在科罗拉多州

925
00:51:06.021 --> 00:51:08.228
training and obsessing.
一边训练，一边沉迷

926
00:51:08.440 --> 00:51:10.522
I was really lonely, honestly.
实话实说，很孤独

927
00:51:11.569 --> 00:51:13.810
I met this girl named Becca.
后来遇到了Becca

928
00:51:14.029 --> 00:51:15.394
[Becca]We started dating.
我们就开始约会了

929
00:51:15.614 --> 00:51:17.980
He was thoughtful and considerate,
他很体贴周到

930
00:51:18.200 --> 00:51:21.158
but from the beginning, it was pretty obvious
不过从一开始，就挺明显

931
00:51:21.370 --> 00:51:25.864
his mind was completely occupied by the Dawn Wall.
他的全部关注是黎明墙

932
00:51:26.083 --> 00:51:27.539
It wasn’t just a climb.
这不是一次简单的攀爬

933
00:51:29.086 --> 00:51:30.872
It was all consuming.
这是全部的投入

934
00:51:32.840 --> 00:51:36.253
We were trying to build a relationship.
我们准备建立稳定关系

935
00:51:36.468 --> 00:51:39.255
But he would go out to Yosemite for months at a time,
但他需要隔一段时间就去优胜美地

936
00:51:39.471 --> 00:51:41.928
giving everything to the Dawn Wall.
把一切都投入到黎明墙

937
00:51:44.643 --> 00:51:48.602
Long For years, Tommy put his whole life on hold
多年以来，Tommy把他的全部生活都后置了

938
00:51:48.814 --> 00:51:52.602
so he could give every last ounce of his body and soul
这样才能把他所有的心身

939
00:51:55.195 --> 00:51:58.232
to this impossible quest.
都投放进这个不可能的探索中

940
00:51:58.449 --> 00:52:01.156
[Kevin] I could never tell if we were wasting our time
我永远也不知道，到底我们是在浪费时间呢

941
00:52:01.368 --> 00:52:04.952
or we were in pursuit of something grand.
还是我们在追求某些崇高的目的

942
00:52:05.164 --> 00:52:06.199
Come on! 加油

943
00:52:10.461 --> 00:52:11.621
[Becca] I’d go out to Yosemite
我也来到优胜美地

944
00:52:11.837 --> 00:52:13.373
and I’d watch him from the meadow.
从草地上举头看他

945
00:52:13.589 --> 00:52:14.954
It looked completely ridiculous.
看起来太荒谬了

946
00:52:15.174 --> 00:52:16.880
Ah, shoot. 嚓

947
00:52:17.092 --> 00:52:20.459
I think we all admire people who are dedicated.
我想我们都对奉献者赞美有加

948
00:52:20.679 --> 00:52:23.421
But at some point, you start to wonder,
但，有时，你会想

949
00:52:23.641 --> 00:52:27.179
where are the lines between dedication and obsession?
奉献和沉迷，之间的界限到底是什么？

950
00:52:30.981 --> 00:52:34.644
[Dad] He was going through emotional agony.
他正在经历情感上的苦难

951
00:52:34.860 --> 00:52:37.476
This climb has been gut wrenching.
攀爬是痛苦的

952
00:52:37.696 --> 00:52:39.857
I want this for him so badly.
我是如此之渴望

953
00:52:40.074 --> 00:52:42.440
[Tommy] Argh! 啊

954
00:52:42.660 --> 00:52:44.525
-[Mom] Oh, he fell off. 吖，掉下来了
-Oh.

955
00:52:44.745 --> 00:52:48.158
[Kelly] Man. I mean, you’ve failed on this thing 800 times.
兄弟，我说，你已经失败800次了

956
00:52:48.374 --> 00:52:51.741
How can you continue to beat your head against this wall?
怎么才能继续头顶着墙攀岩下去呀？

957
00:52:51.960 --> 00:52:53.370
[Kevin]After years of effort,
经年的努力 

958
00:52:53.587 --> 00:52:56.624
it didn’t feel like we were any closer to our dream.
我们甚至都没有更接近梦想一点点

959
00:52:57.591 --> 00:52:59.832
[Becca] He’s worked so hard.
他是这么用心

960
00:53:00.052 --> 00:53:01.792
Why am I crying right now?
我怎么就哭了呢？

961
00:53:02.012 --> 00:53:04.173
This project! Argh!
这个计划，啊

962
00:53:04.390 --> 00:53:05.470
[Dad] This makes me wonder
我想到

963
00:53:05.683 --> 00:53:07.014
if he bit off more than he could chew.
如果他能咬牙顶住，而不是咽下

964
00:53:07.226 --> 00:53:09.387
Oh, it’s so good to have you down.
哎，你能下来真是太棒了

965
00:53:12.022 --> 00:53:14.889
[Tommy] After all this failure, I started to wonder
重重失败以后我开始想

966
00:53:15.109 --> 00:53:18.067
if maybe this climb really was impossible.
这个攀岩真是不可行

967
00:53:19.196 --> 00:53:21.152
Maybe I wasn’t good enough.
也许我还不够厉害

968
00:53:39.007 --> 00:53:41.419
-[Kevin] Morning. 早上好
-[Tommy] Morning. 早上好

969
00:53:45.347 --> 00:53:48.180
[Tom]Tommy and Kevin have been up there, this is their 8th day.
Tommy和Kevin，已经在岩墙上，是第八天了

970
00:53:48.392 --> 00:53:50.257
They’re halfway up the Wall.
他们已经半墙高

971
00:53:50.477 --> 00:53:53.844
They got past 70 mile an hour winds, the ice falls.
他们经历了时速70英里的风暴，落冰

972
00:53:54.064 --> 00:53:55.975
They climbed a lot of difficult rock.
他们爬过许多困难的大石

973
00:53:56.191 --> 00:53:59.058
Now they’ve got today a very hard section to do.
此刻，他们今天要做一件巨难的事

974
00:53:59.278 --> 00:54:01.860
They’re here. They’ve got to go across this traverse.
在这儿，他们要横着穿越窄道

975
00:54:02.072 --> 00:54:04.154
140, I think it is.
我觉得有140 尺

976
00:54:04.366 --> 00:54:08.359
If they can get that done, they’re well on their way.
一旦穿越过去，后面就好办了

977
00:54:11.290 --> 00:54:15.249
[Long] The hardest individual part of this 3,000 foot puzzle
3000英尺迷局之中，最难的个体部分 

978
00:54:15.461 --> 00:54:17.952
is the traverse.
就是横道穿越

979
00:54:18.172 --> 00:54:19.457
The bottom section of the route
线路的底部

980
00:54:19.673 --> 00:54:24.258
follows a vague series of cracks and corners in the rock.
紧接着一系列的岩石缝隙和戳出来的石块

981
00:54:24.470 --> 00:54:29.180
But after 1,000 feet, those cracks and corners dead end.
但1000英尺以后，这些缝隙和石头戳角就隐没了

982
00:54:29.391 --> 00:54:32.258
300 feet to the left, there’s another series of features
左侧的300英尺，才有一串石缝

983
00:54:32.478 --> 00:54:34.434
that angles up to the top.
曲折上升

984
00:54:35.731 --> 00:54:36.937
The trick is,
问题是

985
00:54:37.149 --> 00:54:39.435
how do you traverse this 300 foot blank section
怎么才能通过这300英尺的空白墙面

986
00:54:39.651 --> 00:54:41.607
right in the middle of the Wall?
正正在岩墙中央？

987
00:54:41.820 --> 00:54:43.776
[Kevin] There’s this band of rock
这一岩块

988
00:54:43.989 --> 00:54:45.900
that’s a slightly different color and texture.
从颜色和质地，都有点不一样

989
00:54:46.116 --> 00:54:47.697
[Long] Everything above and below it
之上和之下

990
00:54:47.910 --> 00:54:49.366
is impossible to free climb.
完全无法抱石攀爬

991
00:54:49.578 --> 00:54:51.785
But the composition of that band
可是，就是这一块构造

992
00:54:51.997 --> 00:54:55.034
is such that it has a few holds on it.
结构如此这番，几乎无手可下

993
00:54:55.250 --> 00:54:59.789
[Kevin] Over the last six years, we spent over 100 days
过去的六年里，我们花了一百多天

994
00:55:00.005 --> 00:55:02.212
trying to get across this traverse.
企图横穿窄道

995
00:55:02.424 --> 00:55:04.540
[Tommy] Thousands of tries on that single pitch.
就在这单一的绳距，已经尝试了数千遍

996
00:55:06.011 --> 00:55:08.673
I’ve never done it.
我从未成功

997
00:55:08.889 --> 00:55:10.629
[Kevin] Now we have to do it for the very first time...
现在，我们要第一次跨越

998
00:55:10.849 --> 00:55:13.841
[Tom] Looks like Tommy’s getting ready.
Tommy 看起来准备好了

999
00:55:14.061 --> 00:55:16.427
[Kevin]...in the moment, on the push.
这一刻，出发

1000
00:55:17.648 --> 00:55:18.888
Go get it.
祝成功

1001
00:55:28.826 --> 00:55:30.362
[Tommyl It’s really unnerving.
充满紧张的时刻

1002
00:55:30.577 --> 00:55:32.784
You’re just waiting to slip off at any moment.
任何时间都可能掉下、滑下

1003
00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:43.495
[KeIIy] It’s kind of funny.
有点荒唐可笑

1004
00:55:43.715 --> 00:55:47.207
This 3,000 foot wall, and it’s coming down to millimeters
3千英尺高的岩墙，只有几毫米的地方

1005
00:55:47.427 --> 00:55:50.385
of skin contact on your fingertips.
给指尖的一点点皮肤可以接触

1006
00:55:50.597 --> 00:55:53.760
It becomes such a zoomed-in world.
它几乎就像到了微观世界

1007
00:55:53.976 --> 00:55:56.592
[Kevin] There’s one way to get across,
只有一条路可以通过

1008
00:55:56.812 --> 00:55:59.349
and it is made up of all these little sequences
由最小的单位组成

1009
00:55:59.565 --> 00:56:01.851
that have to be done perfectly.
只有完美无误的动作才能完成

1010
00:56:02.067 --> 00:56:04.023
You miss a hold, it’s impossible.
失去一个握抓，就前功尽弃

1011
00:56:04.236 --> 00:56:05.976
[Tommyl Yeah, dude. 是呀，哥们

1012
00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:08.528
[Kevin] You grab it wrong, it’s impossible.
抓错地方，也一样前功尽弃

1013
00:56:08.740 --> 00:56:09.729
[Tommy] Nice. 好

1014
00:56:12.953 --> 00:56:15.285
[Kevin] We’re trading attempts.
我们正在尝试

1015
00:56:16.582 --> 00:56:19.824
Tommy ties in and just flips that switch.
Tommy 试了进去，接触开始点

1016
00:56:20.043 --> 00:56:21.829
Alright. Go get it, Tommy.
不错，继续，Tommy

1017
00:57:11.595 --> 00:57:13.711
[Tommy] You grab these sharp holds,
抓到这锋利的握抓点

1018
00:57:13.931 --> 00:57:15.467
like razor blades.
就像抓在刀片上

1019
00:57:20.187 --> 00:57:21.427
[Kevin] Come on! 加油

1020
00:57:23.440 --> 00:57:25.351
[Tommy] Span as far as you can.
尽可能展开身体

1021
00:57:27.736 --> 00:57:29.351
[Kevin] Come on!加油哦

1022
00:57:30.614 --> 00:57:32.195
[Tommy] So stretched out.
如此之展开

1023
00:57:46.713 --> 00:57:49.329
I suddenly felt this confidence.
突然我就感到了自信

1024
00:57:53.971 --> 00:57:58.305
I knew exactly how each finger was going onto each hold,
知道每一节手指怎么做到彼此相握

1025
00:57:58.517 --> 00:58:02.726
where the little ripples on the rock were digging into my shoes.
岩石上的碎屑渗透进鞋子里

1026
00:58:14.783 --> 00:58:17.525
After years of working on that pitch,
只要你在这样绳距上多年努力

1027
00:58:17.744 --> 00:58:20.451
it just came together in this amazing, magical way.
它就会以惊人又神奇的方式组合起来

1028
00:58:20.664 --> 00:58:22.200
[Kevin] Yes, come on!
赞，加油

1029
00:58:22.416 --> 00:58:23.781
Come on! 加油

1030
00:58:25.877 --> 00:58:27.083
Whoa! 哇
 
1031
00:58:27.295 --> 00:58:29.331
[Crowd] Whoo! 呼呼

1032
00:58:34.761 --> 00:58:36.501
Ow—ow—ow—ow! 

1033
00:58:36.722 --> 00:58:39.008
[Long] When I heard that Tommy had done pitch 15,
我听到Tommy完成15绳距时

1034
00:58:39.224 --> 00:58:41.931
that was like,“You’ve got to be kidding me!”
几乎以为：这不是开玩笑吧

1035
00:58:44.187 --> 00:58:45.597
For the first time,
第一次

1036
00:58:45.814 --> 00:58:49.147
these guys actually have a shot at maybe doing this thing.
他们俩激起可以完成攀登的希望

1037
00:58:51.653 --> 00:58:53.644
[Kevin] When Tommy got across,
当Tommy完成穿越

1038
00:58:53.864 --> 00:58:55.855
it was a big moment.
真是伟大一刻呀

1039
00:58:56.074 --> 00:58:59.532
Everything was rolling, and now it was my turn.
都可以翻页的，此刻我要去尝试

1040
00:59:08.879 --> 00:59:10.790
Over the years, we realized
过去很多年间，我们都认识到

1041
00:59:11.006 --> 00:59:14.123
sometimes the best conditions are at night.
最佳的攀岩点是夜间

1042
00:59:16.261 --> 00:59:18.172
It’s colder. It’s drier.
既寒冷、又干燥

1043
00:59:18.388 --> 00:59:20.720
So there’s better friction on the rock.
因此岩石的缝隙更合适（抓握）

1044
00:59:22.350 --> 00:59:24.887
At first, it’s scary.
开始时，这挺吓人的

1045
00:59:25.103 --> 00:59:28.561
But after a while, you forget how high off the ground you are
但过一会儿，就会忘记你距离地面的高度

1046
00:59:28.774 --> 00:59:31.811
and you can focus just on the climbing.
于是就能专注在攀爬上

1047
00:59:45.957 --> 00:59:47.868
[Groaning]

1048
00:59:51.129 --> 00:59:52.710
Tried it a few times. 
试过几次

1049
00:59:53.590 --> 00:59:56.582
I wasn’t that close.
无法靠近

1050
00:59:56.802 --> 00:59:59.965
We rappelled back to our camp below the traverse.
我们放绳回到窄道之下的大本营

1051
01:00:01.681 --> 01:00:05.549
I was stoked for Tommy, a little stressed for myself.
我给Tommy做了吃的，自己则挺紧张

1052
01:00:08.522 --> 01:00:11.514
[Long] So Tommy’s made it through the traverse.
这样Tommy就完成了横穿窄道

1053
01:00:11.733 --> 01:00:14.099
He still has to get past the Dyno
他还有 the Dyno 这个绳距要完成

1054
01:00:14.319 --> 01:00:16.651
and the Long Run to Wino Tower.
还有从the Long Run 到 Wino Tower 的绳距
  
1055
01:00:22.285 --> 01:00:25.152
But first, he has to wait for Kevin to catch up.
但首先，他要等Kevin 赶上来

1056
01:00:36.842 --> 01:00:39.333
[Phone rings]

1057
01:00:39.553 --> 01:00:40.963
[Tommy] Hello? 喂

1058
01:00:41.179 --> 01:00:42.589
[Branch]‘Hey, guys. This is John Branch from the NY Times.
嗨，哥们，我是《纽约时报》的John Branch

1059
01:00:42.806 --> 01:00:44.888
-‘How’s it going up there?’ 你们怎样？
-Tommy]Good, John. 挺好，John

1060
01:00:45.100 --> 01:00:47.557
[Branch]‘Tommy, I know that you made it to 15 last night.
Tommy，知道你昨晚完成了15绳距

1061
01:00:47.769 --> 01:00:49.179
‘It’s very exciting,
真令人激动兴奋

1062
01:00:49.396 --> 01:00:51.057
‘so I appreciate you guys taking just a few minutes to talk.’
所以感谢，要花你们几分钟时间来聊一聊

1063
01:00:51.273 --> 01:00:53.389
We’re always looking for stories that are a little bit
我们一直在寻找一些故事

1064
01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:55.064
out of the mainstream sports realm.
不完全是在主流的体育范畴

1065
01:00:55.277 --> 01:00:56.813
Every time we start a hard pitch...
每次开始尝试比较难的绳距

1066
01:00:57.028 --> 01:01:00.395
[Branch]I knew about the Dawn Wall and Tommy Caidwell’s quest.
我知道黎明墙，也知道Tommy Caidwell 的追求

1067
01:01:00.615 --> 01:01:03.698
And when I heard that Tommy did pitch 15, I thought,
听到Tommy完成15绳距的消息，

1068
01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:05.992
if it was ever going to happen, this might be the time.
我想： 如果这件事要发生，那，现在就是它了

1069
01:01:06.204 --> 01:01:07.489
We recognized
我们意识到

1070
01:01:07.706 --> 01:01:09.947
this is not only the best climbing story of the year,
它不仅仅是当年最佳攀岩

1071
01:01:10.167 --> 01:01:11.202
but maybe of our generation.
甚至可能是我们这一代里的最佳攀岩

1072
01:01:11.418 --> 01:01:12.999
‘We talked about follow-up stories.’
我们讨论了后续报道

1073
01:01:13.211 --> 01:01:14.326
Quickly typed up a story.
很快写出报道

1074
01:01:14.546 --> 01:01:17.788
The next day, it ran in the paper.
第二天，就上了新闻

1075
01:01:18.008 --> 01:01:19.839
[Kevin] It was on the front page of The New York Times,
《纽约时报》头版报道

1076
01:01:20.051 --> 01:01:21.382
and it just exploded.
它成了爆炸性新闻

1077
01:01:21.595 --> 01:01:24.553
[Branch] It was the most viewed story at nytimes.com.
也成为 nytimes.com 网站点击率最高的新闻

1078
01:01:24.764 --> 01:01:26.254
Tons of comments. Lots of questions.
雪花般的评论，无穷多的问题

1079
01:01:26.474 --> 01:01:27.259
People care about this.
人们关注它

1080
01:01:27.475 --> 01:01:28.965
[Long] When John Branch,
John Branch 是 

1081
01:01:29.186 --> 01:01:31.518
the Pulitzer Prize winning journalist, got a hold of it,
普利策获奖记者，当他抓到这个报道时，

1082
01:01:31.730 --> 01:01:34.437
it just got its own momentum.
正好抓到了一个最佳点

1083
01:01:34.649 --> 01:01:36.355
And it just got bigger and bigger from there.
此后影响越来越大

1084
01:01:36.568 --> 01:01:38.559
[Kevin] There was follow-up stories
很多后续报道

1085
01:01:38.778 --> 01:01:40.814
and a flood of media requests
潮水一般的媒体

1086
01:01:41.031 --> 01:01:44.068
from every major news outlet in the world.
从世界各大新闻机构报道出来

1087
01:01:44.284 --> 01:01:46.696
[Presenter] Picture this. Our next guests talk to us
想象一下，我们下一位要对话的嘉宾

1088
01:01:46.912 --> 01:01:49.528
as they were suspended high up in mid air.
此刻正悬挂在半空

1089
01:01:49.748 --> 01:01:52.364
[Tommy]‘We’re sitting in a portaledge, which is basically’
我们正坐在悬挂帐篷里

1090
01:01:52.584 --> 01:01:54.916
a hanging cot with an aluminum frame.
悬挂帐篷就是有铝制框架的悬挂小床

1091
01:01:55.128 --> 01:01:57.335
[Presenter] That’s professional climber Tommy CaIdwell
这位专业攀岩家Tommy Caldwell

1092
01:01:57.547 --> 01:01:59.333
ten days into what’s considered
有十天之久

1093
01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:01.961
one of the world’s most daunting climbing challenges.
正在进行被世人认为是世上最令人敬畏之攀岩

1094
01:02:02.177 --> 01:02:03.713
This is crazy.
疯啦

1095
01:02:03.929 --> 01:02:05.135
[Presenter] ‘Best of luck.’祝好运

1096
01:02:05.347 --> 01:02:06.837
Great. Thank you so much. 
好的，谢谢。

1097
01:02:08.558 --> 01:02:10.890
Guess we hang up. I don’t really know.
挂了。其实我不知道

1098
01:02:13.063 --> 01:02:16.772
They don’t tell us what to do when it’s over.
他们并没有告诉我们何时结束

1099
01:02:16.983 --> 01:02:18.519
[Car horn blares]

1100
01:02:18.735 --> 01:02:20.600
[Woman] Oh, my God! 天哪

1101
01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:22.310
How many days does it take?
要多久？

1102
01:02:22.530 --> 01:02:23.861
[Tommy] All of a sudden,
突然之间

1103
01:02:24.074 --> 01:02:26.030
there are crowds of people congregating in the Valley.
大批人群在山谷里开始聚集起来

1104
01:02:26.243 --> 01:02:29.110
Let’s turn now to this historic feat by two American climbers.
让我们转向创造美国攀岩历史的两位

1105
01:02:29.329 --> 01:02:31.160
Perched on a cliff above Yosemite.
栖留在优胜美地的悬崖上

1106
01:02:31.373 --> 01:02:33.864
The famously steep face of El Capitan.
El Capitan 岩墙上最著名的陡峻之地

1107
01:02:34.084 --> 01:02:37.417
The whole media thing was very strange for me.
对我来说，完全不了解媒体

1108
01:02:37.629 --> 01:02:38.960
[Presenter]
The climb of the century.
世纪性攀岩

1109
01:02:39.172 --> 01:02:40.252
it's just been extraordinary
了不起

1110
01:02:40.465 --> 01:02:42.456
A real cliffhanger. Did I just say that?
我是不是该这么说： 真正的悬崖高手

1111
01:02:42.676 --> 01:02:44.587
They were just saying these ludicrous things.
他们用尽赞美的语言

1112
01:02:44.803 --> 01:02:46.213
-Two American hikers. 两位美国户外远足
-Daredevils. 胆大冒险者

1113
01:02:46.429 --> 01:02:47.669
-Thrill seekers. 激动人心的探索者
-Adrenaline junkies. 肾上腺飙高的冒险家

1114
01:02:47.889 --> 01:02:49.800
Scaling the cliff known as El Capitan.
一步步在攀爬 El Capitan 悬崖

1115
01:02:50.016 --> 01:02:51.426
[Tommy] That’s not even El Cap.
这太不像 El Cap了

1116
01:02:51.643 --> 01:02:53.850
Inching up without any climbing tools.
没有任何登山器械，一寸寸的徒手攀岩

1117
01:02:54.062 --> 01:02:56.895
I’m wearing pretty much the same gear as the guys up in Yosemite.
我现在的装备，和优胜美地的那两位几乎一样

1118
01:02:57.107 --> 01:03:00.725
I like the second picture, so we’ll hover here.
我喜欢第二张图，让我们从这里开始

1119
01:03:00.944 --> 01:03:03.560
[Tommy] The Dawn Wall was always this personal journey.
黎明墙本是一趟个人之行

1120
01:03:03.780 --> 01:03:05.486
[Presenter]This was a bad idea.
这想法不成吧

1121
01:03:06.241 --> 01:03:07.526
And obviously,
显而易见

1122
01:03:07.742 --> 01:03:09.607
this turned into something very different from that.
这变得完全不是一回事了

1123
01:03:09.828 --> 01:03:11.659
So don’t understand how they could possibly do it.
完全不懂他们是怎么做到的

1124
01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.736
I hope they make it, but I don’t understand it.
希望他们成功，不过我还是不能理解

1125
01:03:13.957 --> 01:03:14.992
It’s the challenge.
这是挑战

1126
01:03:15.208 --> 01:03:17.665
Yeah, the challenge of it. No. thanks.
是，挑战。不，谢谢（我不会去挑战）

1127
01:03:17.877 --> 01:03:21.119
[Tommy]Suddenly, the whole world was watching this climb.
突然之间，整个世界都像是在观看攀岩

1128
01:03:21.339 --> 01:03:24.923
[Kevin] Which wasn’t the best timing for me personally,
个人而言，不是最佳时机

1129
01:03:27.345 --> 01:03:29.631
because I still had to do pitch 15.
因为我还需要完成15绳距

1130
01:03:31.725 --> 01:03:34.467
[Long]  At this point,they’ve established a base camp
此时，他们已经建立了一个大本营

1131
01:03:34.686 --> 01:03:36.893
a couple of hundred feet below the traverse.
在窄道下面一两百英尺的地方

1132
01:03:37.105 --> 01:03:38.436
So when Kevin’s ready to climb,
所以，Kevin 准备攀爬时

1133
01:03:38.648 --> 01:03:41.264
they go up the fixed ropes to the start of pitch 15.
他们就沿着绳索上升到15绳距的起点

1134
01:03:44.446 --> 01:03:46.778
Tommy sets up his belay,
Tommy 帮他准备好栓绳

1135
01:03:46.990 --> 01:03:50.198
and Kevin tries to get across this thing.
Kevin 就准备窄道横穿

1136
01:03:50.410 --> 01:03:52.776
Here would be actually a big moment on the climb.
这将是攀岩的一个大时刻

1137
01:03:52.996 --> 01:03:54.987
Drove all the way out here today just to see this.
今天一路开车过来，就是想目睹这过程

1138
01:03:57.083 --> 01:04:00.041
[Kevin] It was important to get through pitch 15
穿越15绳距很重要啦

1139
01:04:00.253 --> 01:04:02.369
and catch up to Tommy’s high point
这样可以追上Tommy 的最高攀爬点

1140
01:04:02.589 --> 01:04:04.329
as soon as possible.
尽可能地

1141
01:04:11.556 --> 01:04:13.262
Come on, Key. You got it.
加油，Kevin，你可以的

1142
01:04:19.522 --> 01:04:21.433
Oh!

1143
01:04:21.649 --> 01:04:24.641
[Kevin] Every fall, you go back to the start of the pitch,
每次摔落，都必须回到那个绳距的起点

1144
01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:27.102
rest for at least an hour...
休息至少一个小时

1145
01:04:29.282 --> 01:04:31.113
...try again.
然后继续

1146
01:04:33.870 --> 01:04:36.907
Every attempt, you wear off more skin.
每次尝试，皮肤就被擦掉一些

1147
01:04:37.123 --> 01:04:38.454
You run out of a little more energy.
精力也被慢慢耗掉

1148
01:04:40.001 --> 01:04:41.866
[Reporter 1] Everything was going smoothly
诸事顺利

1149
01:04:42.087 --> 01:04:44.499
until Jorgeson couldn’t grasp pitch 15.
直到 Kevin Jorgeson 无法完成15绳距为止 

1150
01:04:44.714 --> 01:04:46.545
[Reporter 2] Stopped by the sheer difficulty of the climb.
被攀岩的纯难击倒

1151
01:04:46.758 --> 01:04:48.043
[Reporter 3] As the razor-sharp hand holds
当刀锋般的岩石

1152
01:04:48.259 --> 01:04:49.715
tore the skin off his fingertips.
刮去他指尖的皮肤

1153
01:04:49.928 --> 01:04:51.259
[Kevin] So everyone’s tuning in
当大家都关注到

1154
01:04:51.471 --> 01:04:53.553
in the middle of guys living on the side of the Wall...
在岩壁上呆着的两哥们

1155
01:04:53.765 --> 01:04:56.222
[Reporter 4] History is on hold in Yosemite National Park.
优胜美地国家公园正在创造历史

1156
01:04:56.434 --> 01:04:57.799
[Kevin] ...and one of them’s stuck.
有一个人搞砸了

1157
01:04:58.019 --> 01:04:59.384
Argh!

1158
01:04:59.604 --> 01:05:01.936
[Reporter 5]
Kevin Jorgeson is stuck.
Kevin Jorgeson 卡壳了。

1159
01:05:02.148 --> 01:05:04.104
-[Tommy] That was close, dude. 快了，兄弟
-[Kevin] I know. 我知道

1160
01:05:04.317 --> 01:05:07.275
[Tommy] You just started to fall apart a little bit there.
你离开那儿很近才掉下来的

1161
01:05:07.487 --> 01:05:09.569
[Branch] It’s a pretty fascinating drama
这超级戏剧化

1162
01:05:09.781 --> 01:05:13.365
unfolding in real time, literally in front of our eyes.
真实时间就这样展开，简直可以说，就在我们眼前

1163
01:05:13.576 --> 01:05:16.192
People who I’m sure had no idea what a pitch was
对绳距毫无概念的人们

1164
01:05:16.413 --> 01:05:18.745
were now going, “Pitch 15! Come on, Kevin! You can do it!”
现在也念叨着：15绳距，加油，Kevin，你能做到的

1165
01:05:18.957 --> 01:05:21.369
[Groans]

1166
01:05:21.584 --> 01:05:23.449
You’ll get it, dude. That was really close.
你绝对可以的，已经挺近了

1167
01:05:23.670 --> 01:05:26.252
[Tommy] I spent a few days not climbing,
好几天我都没有攀爬

1168
01:05:26.464 --> 01:05:30.002
just belaying Kevin over and over again on pitch 15.
在15绳距那里，一次次帮助Kevin准备栓绳，

1169
01:05:32.262 --> 01:05:33.843
[Groans]

1170
01:05:35.723 --> 01:05:38.806
It was harder than any pitch of climbing he’d ever done.
这比他经历过的所以绳距都要更难

1171
01:05:39.018 --> 01:05:40.599
[Kevin] Fucker! 见鬼

1172
01:05:40.812 --> 01:05:43.554
[Tommy] He just kept falling and falling.
他不停掉下来

1173
01:05:43.773 --> 01:05:46.936
I had honestly started to lose hope that he was going to do it.
我真心失去信心，疑惑他能不能完成

1174
01:05:47.152 --> 01:05:49.814
[Kevin] Last night was my third day
昨天已经是尝试的第三天

1175
01:05:50.029 --> 01:05:52.691
of battle with pitch 15.
这场与15绳距的争斗

1176
01:05:52.907 --> 01:05:57.071
Still didn’t do it.
我还是败了

1177
01:05:57.287 --> 01:06:01.872
After trying so many times, I’ve destroyed my fingers.
试过那么多次以后，手指都磨损了

1178
01:06:02.083 --> 01:06:07.328
So I decided to take a rest day and let my fingers heal.
因此我决定休整一天，恢复手指

1179
01:06:12.886 --> 01:06:16.378
[Long] Meanwhile, Tommy hasn’t climbed for days.
与此同时，Tommy 停止攀岩已经好多天

1180
01:06:17.682 --> 01:06:18.967
And he has to be thinking,
他在想

1181
01:06:19.184 --> 01:06:22.392
I can’t stay up here indefinitely waiting for Kevin.
我不能停在这儿，遥遥无期地等待Kevin

1182
01:06:22.604 --> 01:06:24.595
I mean, there’s very few people in the world
我意思是，世上很少有人

1183
01:06:24.814 --> 01:06:27.726
that have ever even spent that much time on a wall.
在一面岩墙上花这么长时间

1184
01:06:27.942 --> 01:06:30.729
[Tommy] Living on the Wall just wears you down.
住在岩墙上真的很消磨斗志

1185
01:06:30.945 --> 01:06:32.355
It’s just harsh up there.
就是很严酷的啦

1186
01:06:32.572 --> 01:06:34.108
You can’t even walk.
你都没法走一走

1187
01:06:34.324 --> 01:06:36.064
You’re not sleeping great at night.
夜里也睡不好

1188
01:06:36.284 --> 01:06:40.197
You’re not eating normal foods, drinking enough water.
吃不上正常食品，喝水不够

1189
01:06:40.413 --> 01:06:43.701
It’s hard to climb your best under those conditions.
这种条件下，很难发挥攀岩最佳水平

1190
01:06:43.917 --> 01:06:47.284
[Branch] Every day that goes by, maybe Tommy suddenly gets sick.
也许哪一天，Tommy 突然生了病

1191
01:06:47.504 --> 01:06:48.744
Maybe the weather changes.
也许天气突变

1192
01:06:48.963 --> 01:06:52.080
[Tommy] I felt like I had to continue.
我觉得我应该继续前进

1193
01:06:52.300 --> 01:06:54.586
[Long] So they devised a plan.
所以他们重新设置了一个计划

1194
01:06:54.802 --> 01:06:57.384
Tommy’s going to press on and try the Dyno pitch,
Tommy 往下一个绳距 （the Dyno 绳距）进发

1195
01:06:57.597 --> 01:07:00.634
hoping that Kevin eventually will get across 15
同时期待Kevin 最终克服15绳距

1196
01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:02.681
and he can catch up.
然后他可以追赶上来

1197
01:07:02.894 --> 01:07:05.431
[Kevin]That night, we go up our fixed lines
那天夜里，我们出发到已经固定的线路

1198
01:07:05.647 --> 01:07:08.730
and I belay Tommy on pitch 16, the Dyno pitch.
我帮Tommy准备16绳距，the Dyno 绳距

1199
01:07:10.151 --> 01:07:11.391
[Tommy] I had tried the Dyno move
我曾经试过在 Dyno 绳距那里移动 

1200
01:07:11.611 --> 01:07:13.567
hundreds of times over the years.
过去几年间，有上百次吧

1201
01:07:17.825 --> 01:07:18.814
Never done it.
从未成功过

1202
01:07:19.035 --> 01:07:21.902
I’d rebuilt it on the shed at my home,
我在自己家里重建了一个木棚

1203
01:07:22.121 --> 01:07:25.830
so I could just practice this one stupid move.
为了我能够练习这个蠢笨的动作

1204
01:07:26.042 --> 01:07:27.873
Just before we went for our final push
直到出发去最终的攀岩时刻

1205
01:07:28.086 --> 01:07:29.496
I was completely frustrated,
整个人都不好了，崩溃

1206
01:07:29.712 --> 01:07:32.704
staring at these photos of the Wall.
盯着岩墙的这些图片

1207
01:07:32.924 --> 01:07:37.167
I started to notice cracks and edges that go down and around.
我开始关注上下左右的细缝和突角

1208
01:07:37.387 --> 01:07:39.469
So I came up with this idea
于是有了一个想法

1209
01:07:39.681 --> 01:07:42.468
to do the most ridiculous pitch of climbing.
来完成这个最荒谬的攀爬

1210
01:07:42.684 --> 01:07:45.471
[Kevin] His idea was to just climb in a giant circle
他想的是，用大回环的方式爬上去

1211
01:07:45.687 --> 01:07:47.848
around the Dyno. I was like, “Really?”
就是在Dyno绳距那里。我表示说：真的？

1212
01:07:48.064 --> 01:07:49.804
[Brett] So to get around about eight feet...?
就为了这八英尺？

1213
01:07:50.024 --> 01:07:52.606
[Tommy] Yeah, climb like 200.
是呀，要爬200

1214
01:07:52.819 --> 01:07:56.778
Tommy’s currently working out the world’s hardest down climb.
Tommy正在做的是，世上最艰难的下岩

1215
01:07:56.990 --> 01:08:00.733
We do hard moves going straight up, hard moves going sideways.
我们一般是攀上，更难的是水平移动

1216
01:08:00.952 --> 01:08:01.987
I should add a down climb.
我要加上一个下移攀爬动作

1217
01:08:02.203 --> 01:08:04.865
That way, we just get the full package.
这样，我们把攀岩的动作就弄完整了

1218
01:08:06.499 --> 01:08:08.785
Down climbing, it’s so unnatural.
下岩攀爬，是如此不自然

1219
01:08:09.002 --> 01:08:10.117
[Tommyl Falling. 跌

1220
01:08:10.336 --> 01:08:13.169
[Kevin] It’s like running backwards.
这就像往后跑

1221
01:08:15.383 --> 01:08:16.964
[Tommy] That felt horrible.
恐怖

1222
01:08:34.444 --> 01:08:35.980
[Kevin] Good, Tommy.
不错，Tommy

1223
01:08:37.280 --> 01:08:38.861
Nice. 挺棒

1224
01:08:45.705 --> 01:08:47.411
Come on. Focus.
加油，集中注意力

1225
01:08:49.751 --> 01:08:51.116
Good. 赞

1226
01:08:53.296 --> 01:08:54.786
[KeIIy] This loop pitch,
这个回环绳距

1227
01:08:55.006 --> 01:08:58.419
it’s like walking around the block to cross the street.
就好比兜了一圈穿过街道

1228
01:08:58.635 --> 01:09:00.842
It is just a little bit ridiculous.
看起来挺荒唐

1229
01:09:02.305 --> 01:09:04.387
But it’s also kind of brilliant.
但真的是才华横溢

1230
01:09:04.599 --> 01:09:05.805
[Kevin] Come on. 加油

1231
01:09:06.517 --> 01:09:07.677
Come on. 加油啦

1232
01:09:10.021 --> 01:09:11.932
[KeIIy] This thing that had been shutting him down
阻碍他的这个东西

1233
01:09:12.148 --> 01:09:13.388
for all these years,
阻碍了这么多年

1234
01:09:13.608 --> 01:09:17.396
and then he just looks at it with a new set of eyes
然后现在他用一个新的视角去看它

1235
01:09:17.612 --> 01:09:19.728
and finds a new solution.
就找到了新的解决方案

1236
01:09:19.947 --> 01:09:21.483
[Tommy] Yeah. 耶

1237
01:09:21.699 --> 01:09:23.280
The Dyno!

1238
01:09:23.993 --> 01:09:25.949
Whoo! 呜哈哈

1239
01:09:39.050 --> 01:09:40.631
[Tommy] How is the skin, dude?
兄弟，皮肤好些没？

1240
01:09:42.261 --> 01:09:45.253
It’s not healing very quickly,
恢复不快

1241
01:09:45.473 --> 01:09:48.556
which is frustrating.
这一点最令人沮丧

1242
01:09:48.768 --> 01:09:52.852
[Long] While Kevin’s waiting for his fingers to heal,
当Kevin等着他手指复原时

1243
01:09:53.064 --> 01:09:57.057
Tommy continued pushing the route higher and higher.
Tommy 已经把绳距往上推的越来越高

1244
01:09:57.276 --> 01:09:58.812
What you do every day is,
你每天要做的是

1245
01:09:59.028 --> 01:10:00.939
you get to a high point, and then you leave fixed ropes
上到一个更高的绳距，把绳索固定住

1246
01:10:01.155 --> 01:10:02.611
that go back down to the camp.
然后下到大本营

1247
01:10:02.824 --> 01:10:06.066
The next day, you motor back up the ropes to the high point
第二天，开动，把绳索推向另一个高绳距

1248
01:10:06.285 --> 01:10:07.946
and then carry on.
这样不断前行

1249
01:10:08.162 --> 01:10:09.993
So, even though they might be working
因此，尽管他们俩

1250
01:10:10.206 --> 01:10:11.912
on different parts of the Wall,
在岩墙的不同部位忙乎

1251
01:10:12.125 --> 01:10:14.457
they’re doing it together. Kevin belays Tommy,
他们其实是一起搭档的。Kevin 给Tommy 放绳索

1252
01:10:14.669 --> 01:10:18.582
and once Tommy’s done, they both go back down to the camp.
等Tommy完成后，他们俩一起下回到大本营

1253
01:10:21.467 --> 01:10:23.332
[Kevin] Tommy’s just forging on.
Tommy 不断推进着

1254
01:10:32.687 --> 01:10:36.555
Every pitch gets him further away from where I’m stuck.
每一个绳距的前推，都把我卡壳的地方甩的越来越远

1255
01:10:38.025 --> 01:10:39.356
[Tommyl One more down.
接着下去吧

1256
01:10:39.569 --> 01:10:42.060
[Kevin]There’s so much distance between our high points
我们之间的最高绳距，彼此距离越来越远

1257
01:10:42.280 --> 01:10:44.316
that I’m not going to be able to close that gap
我没有可能把这个差距填补上了

1258
01:10:44.532 --> 01:10:46.523
in a reasonable amount of time
在可能的合理时间内

1259
01:10:46.743 --> 01:10:48.324
unless I do this.
除非我已经做到（完成15绳距）

1260
01:10:48.536 --> 01:10:50.527
[Tommy] Every time I would look over in his portaledge
每次我看到他在悬空帐篷里

1261
01:10:50.747 --> 01:10:52.612
he would just be following news updates,
他在看新闻更新

1262
01:10:52.832 --> 01:10:54.743
staring at his fingertips,
一边看他的手指尖

1263
01:10:54.959 --> 01:10:56.369
mumbling to himself.
一边叨叨着什么

1264
01:10:56.586 --> 01:10:59.373
[Kevin] Trying to convince myself these actually look good.
试着说服自己这还是挺好的

1265
01:11:03.217 --> 01:11:04.627
Tommy, do you have the Ibuprofen?
Tommy，你有没有布洛芬？

1266
01:11:06.053 --> 01:11:07.918
Oh, yeah. 有

1267
01:11:08.139 --> 01:11:12.007
[Kevin] After two days resting, I felt resolved.
又休息两天后，我觉得需要有一个了结

1268
01:11:13.269 --> 01:11:15.260
This was the day it had to happen.
该发生的就是该让它发生

1269
01:11:18.232 --> 01:11:19.597
It’s still pretty warm out.
天气还比较暖和

1270
01:11:19.817 --> 01:11:21.682
And so I’m going to wait a few more hours
所以要再等几个钟点

1271
01:11:21.903 --> 01:11:23.518
for the temperatures to drop even more
等温度降下去

1272
01:11:23.738 --> 01:11:26.901
to give myself every bit of friction you can.
给自己尽可能的摩擦力

1273
01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:28.276
[Tommy] You ready? 准备好了没？

1274
01:11:28.493 --> 01:11:31.326
[Kevin] Ready as I’m ever going to be.
像以前一样，准备好了

1275
01:11:52.391 --> 01:11:56.134
I’ve been waiting for days for the skin to heal,
我已经等了多天，等皮肤愈合

1276
01:11:57.522 --> 01:11:59.262
for this moment to come.
等着这一刻来到

1277
01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:10.114
There’s a nice cold breeze blowing up the wall.
凉风轻吹着岩壁

1278
01:12:11.744 --> 01:12:14.201
I felt weightless.
我觉得自己身轻如燕

1279
01:12:14.413 --> 01:12:17.746
I was just floating across the pitch.
我几乎要漂浮过这个绳距

1280
01:12:32.056 --> 01:12:33.637
[Tommy] Hold it together.
抓牢

1281
01:12:40.940 --> 01:12:42.726
[Groans]

1282
01:12:44.610 --> 01:12:46.441
Come on, Kevin. Do it, man.
加油，Kevin，兄弟，做吧

1283
01:12:46.654 --> 01:12:47.894
You got it.
你可以的

1284
01:12:48.781 --> 01:12:50.317
Come on. 加油

1285
01:12:50.533 --> 01:12:52.364
You got it. 快了

1286
01:12:52.577 --> 01:12:53.987
Come on. Find it.
加油，找到那个点

1287
01:12:54.203 --> 01:12:55.739
Good. Come on.
不错。加油啦

1288
01:12:56.622 --> 01:12:58.738
Argh!

1289
01:13:00.251 --> 01:13:02.492
[Tommy] Oh, that was so good, dude.
兄弟，还是挺棒的了

1290
01:13:04.505 --> 01:13:08.965
[Kevin] Everything was perfect, and I still didn’t do it.
万事俱备，结果我还是失败了

1291
01:13:10.511 --> 01:13:11.546
[Matt] Come on, Kevin.
加油，Kevin

1292
01:13:11.762 --> 01:13:13.969
[Kevin] I tried four times that night.
那个晚上我试了四次

1293
01:13:15.266 --> 01:13:16.255
Fucker! 鬼

1294
01:13:16.475 --> 01:13:18.181
[Man] He’s off.
又摔下来了

1295
01:13:18.394 --> 01:13:19.930
[Kevin] I just kept falling.
我不断掉下来

1296
01:13:24.942 --> 01:13:26.022
Shit! 狗屎

1297
01:13:26.777 --> 01:13:28.563
Tonight... 今晚

1298
01:13:30.948 --> 01:13:32.688
...didn’t go so well.
真不顺

1299
01:13:35.119 --> 01:13:38.111
It was a battle, and I didn’t win.
这是战斗，我就是没有赢下来

1300
01:13:38.331 --> 01:13:40.492
It was pretty clear that that was it.
它就像

1301
01:13:40.708 --> 01:13:42.915
Like, you had your chance.
比如，你是有机遇的

1302
01:13:43.127 --> 01:13:45.118
You weren’t good enough.
但你还不够好

1303
01:13:45.338 --> 01:13:47.203
Yeah, it’s pretty fucked.
是呀，真是糟透了。

1304
01:13:49.842 --> 01:13:53.426
Now you’re the guy that almost climbed the Dawn Wall.
此刻你几乎就是要成功登上黎明墙的人了

1305
01:13:53.638 --> 01:13:55.629
So how much did you enjoy that process?
完成这过程的满足度有多少？

1306
01:13:55.848 --> 01:13:57.804
Because that’s all you get.
因为这是你应得的

1307
01:14:04.899 --> 01:14:06.514
[Branch] Editors and I started talking.
我和编辑们讨论

1308
01:14:06.734 --> 01:14:08.565
Is it now time to do a story about what happens
是不是该写出这个故事

1309
01:14:08.778 --> 01:14:10.234
if he doesn’t make it?
但他并没有完成

1310
01:14:10.446 --> 01:14:11.982
We all want happy endings, but as a journalist, you’re like
我们都喜欢大团圆结局，可是，作为记者

1311
01:14:12.198 --> 01:14:13.813
“That’s an incredible story.”
你应该明白，不可思议的故事是什么

1312
01:14:14.033 --> 01:14:16.615
What’s the ethos in climbing?
攀登的精神是什么？

1313
01:14:16.827 --> 01:14:19.284
Do you say, you go ahead without me?
你想问，就这样你自己前进了

1314
01:14:19.497 --> 01:14:20.987
Do you leave a guy behind?
把同伴拉着后面

1315
01:14:21.207 --> 01:14:22.743
Are they having this conversation
他们是否在黑夜中的悬空帐篷里

1316
01:14:22.959 --> 01:14:25.075
in the portaledge at night?
聊过这些？

1317
01:14:26.587 --> 01:14:28.327
[RainfaII]

1318
01:14:37.890 --> 01:14:39.926
This would be nice to check the radar.
查看雷达可能会有用些

1319
01:14:43.646 --> 01:14:47.264
[kevin] The next day, the weather was starting to get bad.
第二天，天气更糟

1320
01:14:49.068 --> 01:14:50.899
And I knew what I needed to do.
我知道我需要做什么

1321
01:14:51.904 --> 01:14:53.360
[Tommy] 20%.

1322
01:14:53.572 --> 01:14:54.903
[Kevin] Today? 今天吗？

1323
01:14:55.116 --> 01:14:57.778
[Tommy] Next like four days.
之后还要有四天

1324
01:14:57.994 --> 01:14:59.905
I’m just going to throw in the towel
我准备撑到 the Towel

1325
01:15:00.121 --> 01:15:02.157
and support Tommy to the top.
支持Tommy 一直到成功登顶

1326
01:15:05.835 --> 01:15:06.915
[Long] From here on out,
从这时候开始

1327
01:15:07.128 --> 01:15:08.618
Kevin’s just going to belay Tommy
Kevin一心帮助Tommy放绳索

1328
01:15:08.838 --> 01:15:10.374
and follow him up the ropes.
跟他上绳索

1329
01:15:12.633 --> 01:15:14.624
So they go up to Tommy’s high point,
所以他们一点点把Tommy 的最高绳距提升

1330
01:15:14.844 --> 01:15:16.926
where he starts up the last hard pitches
直到他通过那几个最艰难的绳距

1331
01:15:17.138 --> 01:15:19.129
of the long run to Wino Tower.
达到Wino Tower

1332
01:15:25.771 --> 01:15:28.387
[Kevin] There I was, watching Tommy
我就在那儿，看着Tommy

1333
01:15:28.607 --> 01:15:30.598
climb with so much confidence
充满信心地攀爬

1334
01:15:30.818 --> 01:15:33.480
toward the completion of this dream.
攀上他的梦圆点

1335
01:15:37.324 --> 01:15:40.657
Even if I can’t do this, I was really happy for Tommy.
即使我自己没有成功，我还是为此替Tommy感到快乐

1336
01:15:44.665 --> 01:15:46.405
What a special moment
一个特别的时刻

1337
01:15:46.625 --> 01:15:48.581
to witness this piece of history.
亲眼目睹这一节历史

1338
01:15:54.592 --> 01:15:57.208
And I was there to help Tommy realize this vision.
我参与去帮助Tommy实现了梦想

1339
01:16:05.311 --> 01:16:08.053
After everything he went through,
他经过的每一步

1340
01:16:10.483 --> 01:16:12.439
so much struggle,
这么多的挣扎

1341
01:16:13.569 --> 01:16:15.855
the injuries, the doubts.
伤痛、疑惑

1342
01:16:17.573 --> 01:16:20.861
For Tommy it was like, this is it.
对于Tommy，就这样了

1343
01:16:25.998 --> 01:16:27.454
Come on, Tommy.
加油，Tommy

1344
01:16:29.877 --> 01:16:31.162
[Tommy] Boom! 碰 

1345
01:16:31.378 --> 01:16:33.118
[Crowd cheers]

1346
01:16:33.339 --> 01:16:35.830
Woo-hoo! Feels good.
呼哈哈，感觉良好

1347
01:16:37.259 --> 01:16:38.669
[Long] I’m down in the meadow
我在草坪上

1348
01:16:38.886 --> 01:16:41.093
watching Tommy trying to get to Wino Tower,
看着Tommy即将到达 Wino Tower

1349
01:16:41.305 --> 01:16:43.842
which is the next big feature above them.
是等待他们的一个大界标

1350
01:16:44.058 --> 01:16:45.844
It’s this mythical landmark
它是神奇的地标

1351
01:16:46.060 --> 01:16:49.018
about two-thirds of the way up El Capitan.
El Capitan 三分之二的分界

1352
01:16:49.230 --> 01:16:53.064
[Kelly] This three foot pedestal 2,000 feet up the Wall.
这个三英尺的石头台基，位于岩墙的2000 英尺高的地点

1353
01:16:53.275 --> 01:16:55.391
[Long] The first horizontal ledge
是整座岩墙上的第一块水平突角

1354
01:16:55.611 --> 01:16:58.774
where you can stand up, sit down, lie down
可以让你站立，坐下，躺下

1355
01:16:58.989 --> 01:17:00.775
on the entire route.
在整个线路上

1356
01:17:00.991 --> 01:17:04.108
[Kelly] And it signifies the end of the hardest climbing.
它意味着艰苦攀岩过程的结束

1357
01:17:06.664 --> 01:17:08.780
[Tommy] One more hard pitch to get to Wino Tower.
到达Wino Tower之前，还有一个苦逼绳距

1358
01:17:08.999 --> 01:17:10.455
That’s crazy!
真是疯狂啊

1359
01:17:10.668 --> 01:17:14.456
For years, I’d envisioned this moment of getting to Wino Tower.
好多年来，我都在臆想登上Wino Tower那一刻

1360
01:17:14.672 --> 01:17:16.128
So I’m freaking out inside.
内心深处都沸腾了

1361
01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:17.830
[Kevin] Good, Tommy. Come on.
赞，Tommy，加油

1362
01:17:18.050 --> 01:17:21.258
[Tommy] Climbing really tense and kind of shaking nervous.
爬的紧张，神经都颤抖了

1363
01:17:21.470 --> 01:17:22.801
[Kevin] Keep breathing, dude.
保持呼吸，哥们

1364
01:17:28.978 --> 01:17:30.184
Come on. 再加油

1365
01:17:32.189 --> 01:17:33.178
Good. 好

1366
01:17:37.278 --> 01:17:40.020
[Tommy] Just trying to calm myself down enough
需要自我镇定住

1367
01:17:40.239 --> 01:17:42.651
to make it through the final last little bit.
直到通过最后那几块

1368
01:17:48.914 --> 01:17:50.370
[Kevin] Yeah! 耶

1369
01:18:06.390 --> 01:18:08.176
[Howls] Ow! 嗷

1370
01:18:17.860 --> 01:18:19.316
[Sighsl

1371
01:18:20.821 --> 01:18:22.857
[Laughs]

1372
01:18:23.073 --> 01:18:25.439
[Tommy] Oh! I feel a little shaky.
觉得自己都发抖了

1373
01:18:25.659 --> 01:18:27.445
Yeah, I might pass out.
是，快昏过去了

1374
01:18:32.166 --> 01:18:34.122
I can’t believe I’m here right now.
真不敢相信我已经在这儿了

1375
01:18:43.928 --> 01:18:47.671
I know it’s not over yet, but that’s big.
虽然知道还不是最后终点，但这是一大步

1376
01:18:48.933 --> 01:18:50.514
I’m at Wino Tower.
我在 Wino Tower

1377
01:18:59.276 --> 01:19:01.892
[Brett] What are you feeling?
感觉如何？

1378
01:19:02.112 --> 01:19:05.070
I want Kevin to experience this, too. for sure.
毫无疑问，我希望Kevin也能经历这个

1379
01:19:09.328 --> 01:19:11.068
[Tommy] It was this huge victory.
这是巨大的胜利

1380
01:19:11.288 --> 01:19:12.778
But it’s totally trumped by the fact
但却被一个事实压倒

1381
01:19:12.998 --> 01:19:15.489
that Kevin wasn’t going to do it with me.
就是Kevin没能和我一起

1382
01:19:15.709 --> 01:19:17.916
Suddenly, I just felt alone.
一刹那间，我觉得很孤独

1383
01:19:19.255 --> 01:19:21.587
I think Kevin probably did, too.
我想Kevin也会有同样的感觉

1384
01:19:25.886 --> 01:19:28.548
What a crazy experience this has been.
这是多离奇的一种经历

1385
01:19:29.890 --> 01:19:31.596
It crashed down on me
我脑子里翻滚着一个想法

1386
01:19:31.809 --> 01:19:35.677
that going to the top without Kevin was gonna be devastating.
如果没有Kevin一起登顶，这事就全砸了。

1387
01:19:35.896 --> 01:19:37.727
Just got to get KJ up here now.
要把他弄上来，此刻

1388
01:19:38.983 --> 01:19:40.473
So I decided in that moment
所以在那一刻我决定了

1389
01:19:40.693 --> 01:19:43.355
that we were going to get to the top together.
我们要一起登顶

1390
01:19:43.570 --> 01:19:46.778
-[Brett] What will you do?         你要怎么做？
-Everything I can to help him.     尽全力帮他上来

1391
01:19:46.991 --> 01:19:48.276
Yeah. 是的

1392
01:19:48.492 --> 01:19:51.859
I’m going to go into full-on support mode.
我准备进入全力支持的模式

1393
01:19:54.665 --> 01:19:58.408
[Kevin] That night, we both go back down to the camp.
那一晚，我们都下来到大本营

1394
01:20:02.214 --> 01:20:03.624
We were cooking dinner.
做饭

1395
01:20:03.841 --> 01:20:06.583
It was real quiet.
周围静悄悄的

1396
01:20:06.802 --> 01:20:09.919
And I knew it was this emotional moment for Tommy.
我知道这一刻的Tommy心情激动

1397
01:20:11.849 --> 01:20:14.636
But he’s not very good at verbalizing.
但他不善表达


1398
01:20:16.149 --> 01:20:25.636
I want to do this thing with you, yeah, it's like ...it's cool, man
我希望和你一起登上去，呃，就是 ...真的挺棒，老弟

1399
01:20:30.149 --> 01:20:37.536
I mean, it's awesome but when I take, I just really want you. ...there
Yeah, I do
我意思是，登上去是挺棒，不过，我还是特希望你也在
明白。

1398
01:20:37.916 --> 01:20:39.907
Yeah.
是啊，

1399
01:20:40.127 --> 01:20:43.540
[Kevin]Tommy just told me, in classic Tommy style,
Tommy 以典型的Tommy 风格跟我说

1400
01:20:43.756 --> 01:20:48.500
I don’t care how long it takes for you to get through pitch 15,
我不在意你需要花多久才能通过15绳距

1401
01:20:48.719 --> 01:20:51.426
because I can’t imagine a worse outcome
因为我不能想象那个糟糕的结果

1402
01:20:51.638 --> 01:20:53.469
than doing this alone.
独自一人去登顶

1403
01:20:55.184 --> 01:20:56.765
I don’t want to hold you back, is the thing.
是这样，我不希望你掉在后面

1404
01:20:56.977 --> 01:21:00.265
You’re three days from the top now or some shit.
你离开峰顶就三天时间了

1405
01:21:05.069 --> 01:21:06.650
[Kevin] It’s a pretty special moment.
这一刻很特殊

1406
01:21:09.323 --> 01:21:10.483
I know I can do that pitch.
我知道我能穿过那个绳距

1407
01:21:10.699 --> 01:21:12.735
Yeah, for sure.
是呀，肯定的

1408
01:21:12.951 --> 01:21:16.443
And I feel like if I can do that pitch, I’d be so fucking psyched
我觉得自己可以完成那个绳距，我就是紧张死

1409
01:21:16.663 --> 01:21:17.903
that there’s nothing
没有什么

1410
01:21:18.123 --> 01:21:20.364
that’s going to stop me between there and the top.
可以挡在峰顶和那块地方之间

1411
01:21:20.584 --> 01:21:22.700
I think that’s true.
我认为就是这样

1412
01:21:22.920 --> 01:21:24.581
Just keep stretching. Make sure...
伸展胳膊，确认

1413
01:21:24.797 --> 01:21:27.834
I think I need to do some arm lengthening stretches.
我觉得自己需要把胳膊抻的更长

1414
01:21:28.050 --> 01:21:31.463
[Kevin] So we decided that I would rest two consecutive days
于是我们决定，我再加两天连贯的休息

1415
01:21:31.678 --> 01:21:33.259
so that my skin could heal
等待我皮肤复原

1416
01:21:33.472 --> 01:21:34.962
and try again.
然后再尝试

1417
01:21:37.434 --> 01:21:39.425
[Long] The idea of Tommy waiting,
Tommy 想出来的这个念头

1418
01:21:39.645 --> 01:21:41.727
to risk your own success
冒着自己不成功的限

1419
01:21:41.939 --> 01:21:45.306
in the hopes that maybe by some miracle Kevin can do it,
以期待，也许Kevin可以奇迹般完成穿越

1420
01:21:45.526 --> 01:21:46.936
that’s a partner right there.
这就是同伴的概念

1421
01:21:47.903 --> 01:21:50.736
Coffee for KJ.
为Kevin喝彩

1422
01:21:50.948 --> 01:21:53.655
[Long] But there’s no guarantee that Kevin’s ever gonna make it.
但，Kevin能否做到，谁也不能保证

1423
01:21:53.867 --> 01:21:57.906
I mean, I thought that Kevin was maybe not going to make it.
我意思是，我认为Kevin也许就是做不到

1424
01:21:58.122 --> 01:22:00.078
And I was hoping that,
我也希望

1425
01:22:00.290 --> 01:22:02.155
since this had been a dream of Tommy’s
因为这是Tommy长久的梦想

1426
01:22:02.376 --> 01:22:04.583
a lot longer than it had been a dream of Kevin’s,
比它也成为Kevin的梦想时间要长的多

1427
01:22:04.795 --> 01:22:08.253
that Tommy would find a way to complete this climb.
Tommy可以顺利完成这次攀登

1428
01:22:08.465 --> 01:22:10.922
As Tommy’s friend, selfishly,
从Tommy朋友自私的角度

1429
01:22:11.135 --> 01:22:13.000
I’m thinking to myself, like,
我自己想

1430
01:22:13.220 --> 01:22:16.087
“Kevin, dude, time to throw in the towel and support Tommy.”
Kevin，哥们，是时间去帮助Tommy攀上去

1431
01:22:16.306 --> 01:22:19.093
Somebody less gracious than Tommy CaIdwell might have said,
没有Tommy Caldwell那样仁厚的人会这样说

1432
01:22:19.309 --> 01:22:21.015
“I’ve got to go on without you.”
虽然没有你，我还是要前行

1433
01:22:21.228 --> 01:22:23.640
[Dad] But he was committed to Kevin.
但是他承诺Kevin

1434
01:22:23.856 --> 01:22:25.346
“We’re doing this together.”
我们要一起完成

1435
01:22:25.566 --> 01:22:30.356
And he wouldn’t have been Tommy if he’d done it any other way.
如果不是这样，那就不是Tommy了

1436
01:22:30.571 --> 01:22:32.357
[Reporter 1] This just in. Those two American climbers...
进入报道。两位美国攀岩者

1437
01:22:32.573 --> 01:22:35.110
-[Re porter 2] Kevin Jorgeson.
-[Reporter 3] Kevin Jorgeson.

1438
01:22:35.325 --> 01:22:36.906
[Reporter 4] Stuck for seven straight days.
连续七天时间卡壳了

1439
01:22:37.119 --> 01:22:38.404
[Reporter 5] CaIdwell determined to wait...
Tommy Caldwell 决定等待

1440
01:22:38.620 --> 01:22:39.735
[Reporter 6] One of them refusing to move higher
他们其中一人拒绝独自登高

1441
01:22:39.955 --> 01:22:42.162
without his partner stuck below.
如果他卡壳的搭档无法上去的话

1442
01:22:42.374 --> 01:22:43.489
So will they make it?
所以，他们能成功吗？

1443
01:22:43.709 --> 01:22:45.415
Can you imagine? This really is no joke.
你可以想象吗？这不是开玩笑

1444
01:22:45.627 --> 01:22:47.242
[Kelly] The media started to sound like a tabloid.
媒体开始像小报一样八卦起来

1445
01:22:47.463 --> 01:22:49.579
Is Jorgeson spoiling Tommy’s dreams?
Kevin 会不会毁了Tommy的梦想？

1446
01:22:49.798 --> 01:22:53.541
[Reporter 7]  Down below, the crowd is waiting and watching.
山底下，人群在等待又观望

1447
01:22:55.971 --> 01:22:58.508
[Kevin] Hey, Tommy, what’s the weather look like?
嗨，Tommy， 天气怎么样？

1448
01:22:58.724 --> 01:23:01.636
Oh, wait. That’s right, you dropped your phone.
哦，等等，对了，你把手机弄丢了

1449
01:23:01.852 --> 01:23:03.558
Dropped my phone last night.
昨晚丢的

1450
01:23:03.770 --> 01:23:06.762
I had my chest pocket unzipped. It just fell out.
我的胸兜拉链开了，手机掉出去了。

1451
01:23:06.982 --> 01:23:09.348
Hopefully, I didn’t kill anybody down there.
希望没砸到下面的谁

1452
01:23:09.568 --> 01:23:11.183
I’d heard that Tommy dropped his phone, and I said,
我听到Tommy 掉了手机的事儿，我就说

1453
01:23:11.403 --> 01:23:12.939
“Did he really drop his phone?
他真的掉了手机？

1454
01:23:13.155 --> 01:23:15.316
“Or is he just saying, don’t call me anymore?”
还是，他意思是，别电话我了

1455
01:23:15.532 --> 01:23:18.148
So fed up with the media circus.
被一堆媒体围住

1456
01:23:18.368 --> 01:23:20.199
I think he didn’t drop it.
我觉得他不是掉了手机

1457
01:23:20.412 --> 01:23:22.698
He threw it off.
他是扔了手机

1458
01:23:22.915 --> 01:23:26.248
Yup. Guess we’ve got to just enjoy the view now.
好吧，猜猜我们现在是不是应该欣赏下风景呢

1459
01:23:29.796 --> 01:23:31.411
[Kevin] Over the next few days,
之后的几天

1460
01:23:31.632 --> 01:23:35.170
Tommy was content right where we were,
Tommy 满足于我们所处的位置

1461
01:23:35.385 --> 01:23:37.376
for however long it was going to be.
也不管还需要多久

1462
01:23:38.847 --> 01:23:40.587
He’s just stoked to be up there,
他就是稳稳在上面

1463
01:23:40.807 --> 01:23:43.389
and it’s no big deal if it takes another rest day or two
再花个一天、两天，也不是大事儿

1464
01:23:43.602 --> 01:23:45.638
or three or five or whatever.
或三天、五天，管它去呢

1465
01:23:45.854 --> 01:23:48.436
[Tommy] Yeah, I feel like I’ve just been appreciating things
是呀，我感觉我正在欣赏

1466
01:23:48.649 --> 01:23:51.391
a little bit more the last few days.
比过去几天更会欣赏周边了

1467
01:23:52.486 --> 01:23:54.522
Ah, sun. 噢，太阳出来了

1468
01:23:54.738 --> 01:23:57.650
[Branch] Tommy basically said, “No hurry. I’m patient.”
Tommy 基本就是表述道：不急，我耐心极了

1469
01:23:57.866 --> 01:24:00.403
They’re going to get through it. Don’t freak out.
他们会通过的。别一惊一乍的

1470
01:24:00.619 --> 01:24:02.780
Don’t worry about the rest of the world that’s watching.
别管那个盯着你的世界

1471
01:24:02.996 --> 01:24:04.486
Let’s tune them out. It’s just you and me.
我们忘了他们。就关注你我

1472
01:24:04.706 --> 01:24:05.912
It became the two of them.
这就变成了两个搭档的世界

1473
01:24:06.124 --> 01:24:08.911
I think I have to try to front-step more,
我在想，要不要试试前跨步多一点

1474
01:24:09.127 --> 01:24:12.585
because when it comes time to step on that middle foot,
因为轮到走中间步伐时

1475
01:24:12.798 --> 01:24:15.005
I can’t front-step it or in-step it cos this foot’s in the way.
我就做不到前跨步，或者是叠跨步，因为这只脚挡住了路

1476
01:24:15.217 --> 01:24:16.457
A couple of your falls last time
上回，你摔下来的几次

1477
01:24:16.677 --> 01:24:18.542
were just cos you couldn’t find that right foot.
就是你没能找到放脚的正确位置

1478
01:24:18.762 --> 01:24:20.798
So even if it’s a little bit harder, it’s going to be better.
所以，即使更难，其实也会更好些

1479
01:24:21.014 --> 01:24:26.179
[Kevin] Tommy’s attitude helped take a bit of the pressure off.
Tommy的态度，帮助把压力卸去不少

1480
01:24:26.395 --> 01:24:30.764
But I was still gonna have to do the hardest thing I’ve ever done
但是，还是需要自己去完成平生最难的事

1481
01:24:30.983 --> 01:24:32.974
for this to end well.
去得到一个好结果

1482
01:24:36.154 --> 01:24:37.314
[TV] Trying to make history
试图开创历史

1483
01:24:37.531 --> 01:24:39.613
on one of the hardest climbs in the world.
这是世界上最难的一攀

1484
01:24:39.825 --> 01:24:41.281
TJ, what’s the story?
进展如何？

1485
01:24:41.493 --> 01:24:42.903
[TJ]Here’s the story.
故事在这儿

1486
01:24:43.120 --> 01:24:45.987
I’m only about 30 feet up, and I’ve called my momma twice.
我才上升了30英尺，已经给我妈打过两次电话了

1487
01:24:46.206 --> 01:24:47.412
Airight? Can you imagine?
好吧，你可以想象吗？

1488
01:24:47.624 --> 01:24:49.330
I’m on what’s called a portaledge
我正在所谓的悬空帐篷里

1489
01:24:49.543 --> 01:24:50.908
that’s secured to this wall.
它扣在墙里

1490
01:24:51.128 --> 01:24:53.164
These two climbers are using one of these
他们两位攀岩者就是用这法子

1491
01:24:53.380 --> 01:24:56.042
secured to a flat surface.
扣出一块平整的面

1492
01:24:56.258 --> 01:24:58.169
They’re having to sleep on one of these things,
他们要睡在这平面上

1493
01:24:58.385 --> 01:25:00.671
for weeks possibly, trying to make an impossible climb.
或许，好几个星期。这样来完成不可能的攀岩

1494
01:25:00.887 --> 01:25:03.845
And me? I have holds here I can use to climb the wall.
我呢，我抓住这儿就可以爬墙了

1495
01:25:04.057 --> 01:25:06.594
[Reporter] Scaling the jagged cliff known as El Capitan...
沿着崎岖的El Capitan的悬崖而上........

1496
01:25:06.810 --> 01:25:08.471
[Becca] Who is that, Fitz?
Fitz，这是谁呀？

1497
01:25:08.687 --> 01:25:10.518
-Daddy. -[Becca]Daddy.
爹爹。。。。爹爹

1498
01:25:10.731 --> 01:25:13.393
Getting on the airplane.
登机了

1499
01:25:15.694 --> 01:25:17.104
Fitz and I have been home
我和Fitz在家里

1500
01:25:17.321 --> 01:25:21.030
waiting for our moment to get on a plane and get out here.
等着飞机过来的时候

1501
01:25:21.241 --> 01:25:23.357
And it’s finally come. We’re here.
终于到了。我们来啦

1502
01:25:24.703 --> 01:25:27.285
Hey, Fitz, do you see way up high on El Cap?
嗨，Fitz，你能看到El Cap上面的路吗？

1503
01:25:27.497 --> 01:25:29.613
-Yeah. 能
-Yeah? Can you see Daddy? 能呀？那你能看到爹爹吗？

1504
01:25:29.833 --> 01:25:31.289
[Tommy] After failing for so many years,
这么多年，有多次摔下来的时候

1505
01:25:31.501 --> 01:25:34.413
there was times when I definitely felt like giving up.
我肯定有过放弃的想法

1506
01:25:34.630 --> 01:25:38.122
But it was actually Becca who helped me to keep going.
但Becca一直鼓舞我走下去

1507
01:25:38.342 --> 01:25:40.173
[Becca] Seeing him in his element,
看到他进入状态

1508
01:25:40.385 --> 01:25:43.673
I saw this focus and this purpose.
我看到这种专注和目标

1509
01:25:43.889 --> 01:25:45.629
I really respected him.
我尊重他

1510
01:25:45.849 --> 01:25:48.431
And we fell in love.
也彼此相爱

1511
01:25:48.644 --> 01:25:52.057
[Tommy] Becca became my biggest supporter.
Becca 成了我最大的支持者

1512
01:25:52.272 --> 01:25:53.478
[Becca] We got married.
我们结婚了

1513
01:25:53.690 --> 01:25:56.557
And then we got pregnant shortly after.
很快就怀孕了

1514
01:25:57.861 --> 01:25:58.896
Hi.

1515
01:25:59.112 --> 01:26:01.398
[Tommy] We had a little boy named Fitz.
有了一个男孩 ， Fitz

1516
01:26:01.615 --> 01:26:03.947
[Becca] Hi. Fitz.

1517
01:26:04.159 --> 01:26:07.242
[Tommy] The first day that I had this little baby in my arms,
当我第一次手抱这个小宝贝时

1518
01:26:07.454 --> 01:26:09.695
I was overcome with the emotion.
真是激动万分

1519
01:26:09.915 --> 01:26:13.578
I thought, how am I going to be a good example to Fitz?
我在想，怎样做Fitz的榜样？

1520
01:26:13.794 --> 01:26:16.285
How great it is to be a CaIdwell boy.
成为Caldwell家的孩子真是很棒

1521
01:26:18.590 --> 01:26:21.502
[Becca] Tommy had always viewed his dad as a superhero,
Tommy 一直把父亲看成是超级英雄

1522
01:26:21.718 --> 01:26:26.052
and he wanted to be a superhero for Fitz.
他也期待自己成为Fitz的超级英雄

1523
01:26:26.264 --> 01:26:29.973
[Tommy] I wanted Fitz to look at me with that same sort of awe.
我希望Fitz看着我的时候，也用一种起敬的眼神

1524
01:26:34.690 --> 01:26:38.057
I wanted to show Fitz how to be passionate...
我想要展示给Fitz如何具有热诚

1525
01:26:38.276 --> 01:26:39.311
Boom! 拼

1526
01:26:39.528 --> 01:26:40.893
...and how to dream big.
 ....... 如何怀有大梦想

1527
01:26:41.113 --> 01:26:42.478
He already does.
他已经学会了

1528
01:26:42.698 --> 01:26:44.188
[Tommy] The Dawn Wall embodied that.
黎明墙就是象征

1529
01:26:44.408 --> 01:26:47.320
And so it made me want it even more.
所以它令我更加渴望

1530
01:26:47.536 --> 01:26:49.948
[Becca] I told him, you can’t stop now.
我和他说，你不能现在就停下来

1531
01:26:50.163 --> 01:26:52.575
You have to do everything to make this happen.
你要去尽力实现它

1532
01:26:58.755 --> 01:27:03.419
[Tommy] One, two, three, four, five.
12345

1533
01:27:12.060 --> 01:27:13.425
[Kevin] Sometimes you zoom out
有时，你退出来

1534
01:27:13.645 --> 01:27:17.137
and you think about what a process it’s been,
去想，这是一个怎样的过程

1535
01:27:17.357 --> 01:27:20.269
this wild six-year journey with Tommy.
和Tommy在一起的狂野六年征程

1536
01:27:20.485 --> 01:27:22.146
[Becca] Did Kevin start already?
Kevin已经出发了吗？

1537
01:27:22.362 --> 01:27:25.604
[Kevin] And now here we are
现在我们来了

1538
01:27:25.824 --> 01:27:27.564
at the moment of truth.
一个真实的时间

1539
01:27:27.784 --> 01:27:30.400
[Gail] And we’ve just been mesmerized.

我们像被催眠了

1540
01:27:30.620 --> 01:27:33.202
Hard to put into words something so big.
难以用言语形容

1541
01:27:33.415 --> 01:27:35.030
He’s not going to give up.
他不会放弃的

1542
01:27:57.939 --> 01:27:59.304
[Tommy] I couldn’t imagine
我无法想象

1543
01:27:59.524 --> 01:28:03.062
what he must have been going through at that moment.
那一刻他经历什么样的心情

1544
01:28:33.642 --> 01:28:36.133
[Kevin]I don’t remember the first 50 feet of that pitch.
我都记不得绳距最初的50尺

1545
01:28:42.901 --> 01:28:44.732
[Tommy I watched him go into the section
看着他走到那一块地方

1546
01:28:44.945 --> 01:28:47.061
where he had fallen so many times.
那块他摔下去N次的地方

1547
01:28:47.280 --> 01:28:49.271
I just hold my breath.
我摒住呼吸

1548
01:29:02.504 --> 01:29:04.540
[Kevin] You pull as hard as you can.
尽力拉着自己

1549
01:29:08.176 --> 01:29:09.666
Move your feet.
移动脚步

1550
01:29:13.974 --> 01:29:16.841
Argh 啊

1551
01:29:17.060 --> 01:29:19.096
You’re just trying not to tip over backwards.
脚尖必须尽力不往后移

1552
01:29:24.317 --> 01:29:26.603
Put the heel on.
把足跟拉上

1553
01:29:26.820 --> 01:29:28.560
Slide the hand up.
手掌翻上去

1554
01:29:28.780 --> 01:29:30.771
Take the heel off.
放下足跟

1555
01:29:30.991 --> 01:29:32.447
Drop the right hand in.
放入右手

1556
01:29:33.410 --> 01:29:35.196
Heel back on.
回进足跟

1557
01:29:35.412 --> 01:29:36.902
Left hand down.
左手放下

1558
01:29:41.793 --> 01:29:43.533
Heart rate starts to go up.
心律加快

1559
01:29:46.464 --> 01:29:48.830
[Tommy] My adrenaline starts going cos he’s still hanging on
我的肾上腺素都升高起来，因为他还挂在那儿

1560
01:29:49.050 --> 01:29:51.917
in this place that he had fallen so many times.
挂在这块他摔倒N次的地方

1561
01:30:32.469 --> 01:30:34.084
[Tommy] Yeah, Kevin!
不错，Kevin

1562
01:30:36.473 --> 01:30:38.714
Yeah! 耶呼

1563
01:30:39.643 --> 01:30:40.473
Yes! 对了

1564
01:30:40.685 --> 01:30:42.391
[Crowd cheering]

1565
01:30:46.775 --> 01:30:49.517
[Tommy] Watching him do it, I was just awestruck.
眼望他成功，我都肃然起敬了

1566
01:30:49.736 --> 01:30:52.819
I was like, I can’t believe that just happened.
我就是，嗯，我不敢相信刚才发生的

1567
01:30:54.324 --> 01:30:55.655
He did it.
他成功了

1568
01:30:55.867 --> 01:30:58.358
Freaking guy actually did this thing, right?
崩溃孩子终于成功了，对不对？

1569
01:30:58.578 --> 01:31:00.819
You’re like, “What?”
你表现成: 啥？

1570
01:31:02.624 --> 01:31:04.034
[Reporter 1]   After seven days,
七天以后

1571
01:31:04.250 --> 01:31:06.616
Jorgeson got past the most difficult...
Jorgeson 终于穿越过

1572
01:31:06.836 --> 01:31:09.418
[Reporter 2]Past the toughest section of the climb.
攀岩中最艰难的部位

1573
01:31:09.631 --> 01:31:10.871
[Branch] Yes, he made it.
是的，他成功了

1574
01:31:11.091 --> 01:31:12.581
And now it’s upward.
剩下来就是往上进发

1575
01:31:12.801 --> 01:31:15.338
And you start thinking, are his fingers OK? Can he do 16, 17?
你也会想，他手指还行吗？ 能不能穿过16、17 绳距

1576
01:31:16.096 --> 01:31:17.506
Is this over yet?
这完了吗？

1577
01:31:17.722 --> 01:31:20.134
[Kevin] I had just finished the hardest pitch of my life,
我才完成了一生中最难的绳距

1578
01:31:20.350 --> 01:31:21.965
and I couldn’t even celebrate.
还不到庆祝的时候

1579
01:31:22.185 --> 01:31:24.346
I just need to catch up.
要追赶上去

1580
01:31:24.562 --> 01:31:26.393
[Long] The next pitch is this big Dyno
下一绳距就是大大的Dino 绳距

1581
01:31:26.606 --> 01:31:28.096
that’s so hard that Tommy can’t do it,
即使当时Tommy都没能做到的那个绳距

1582
01:31:28.316 --> 01:31:29.556
he’s got to climb around it.
他是绕圈上去的

1583
01:31:29.776 --> 01:31:31.061
[Kevin] There’s no way in hell
没一点儿门

1584
01:31:31.277 --> 01:31:33.893
that I’m going to try Tommy’s crazy loop pitch.
我会去试试Tommy那个怪异的环形绳距

1585
01:31:34.114 --> 01:31:38.483
So that same night I start trying the 8 and 1/2 foot Dyno.
所以，同一个夜里，我开始尝试 Dyno 绳距的

1586
01:31:39.411 --> 01:31:41.026
Argh! 啊啊

1587
01:31:41.246 --> 01:31:43.237
[Groaning]

1588
01:31:50.422 --> 01:31:51.753
Yeah! 耶哈

1589
01:31:51.965 --> 01:31:55.708
[Long] Kevin, through some kind of magic or levitation,
Kevin，依靠某种神奇或者是浮力

1590
01:31:55.927 --> 01:31:59.795
actually does this Dyno that Tommy was never able to do.
居然用Tommy没法完成的动作，把Dyno 拿下来了

1591
01:32:00.015 --> 01:32:02.131
-[Tommy] So good. 棒极了
-[Reporter 1] Tonight, Kevin... 今晚，Kevin

1592
01:32:02.350 --> 01:32:04.841
[Reporter 2]...now just a few hundred feet behind Caidwell.
只落在Tommy Caidwell后面几百英尺了

1593
01:32:05.061 --> 01:32:07.302
[Kevin] All these hard pitches just keep coming.
后面的超难绳距一一露面

1594
01:32:07.522 --> 01:32:09.058
17. 18. 19.

1595
01:32:09.274 --> 01:32:10.810
[Groansl

1596
01:32:11.026 --> 01:32:13.688
[Tommy] It was like a fight to the death.
它就像是与死神的搏斗

1597
01:32:14.863 --> 01:32:16.353
-[Kevin] Oh, no.不要
-[Brett] Rock! 岩块呀

1598
01:32:16.573 --> 01:32:17.983
That is a bad hold to rip off.
抓握错误，就功亏一篑

1599
01:32:18.199 --> 01:32:19.439
Oh, man. 呕，老兄

1600
01:32:19.659 --> 01:32:22.366
[Tommy]I think it’s a lot harder now.
我想现在还是挺难的

1601
01:32:22.579 --> 01:32:24.285
That didn’t take him too long to figure it out.
他没多久就明白了

1602
01:32:24.497 --> 01:32:25.577
[Brett] Nice, KJ! 赞一个，Kevin

1603
01:32:25.790 --> 01:32:27.496
[Tommy] It’s just a little more tension.
有点紧张感

1604
01:32:27.709 --> 01:32:31.622
Like we need more of that on this route.
好比我们在这条路径上需要这些似的

1605
01:32:31.838 --> 01:32:34.124
[Kevin] The last pitch getting to Wino Tower,
到距离Wino Tower前最后的绳距时

1606
01:32:34.340 --> 01:32:37.628
this crazy fog came in.
起了诡异的浓雾

1607
01:32:37.844 --> 01:32:39.425
[Tommy] Kevin sends this pitch right now,
Kevin 立刻出发了

1608
01:32:39.637 --> 01:32:41.844
he’s going to be caught up with me.
他要赶上我

1609
01:32:49.647 --> 01:32:50.636
[Kevin]Yes! 是了

1610
01:32:50.857 --> 01:32:52.188
[Tommy] Nice one, Kevin. 好好好，Kevin

1611
01:32:52.400 --> 01:32:54.937
[Kevin]I just remember seeing Tommy at the anchor
我还记得在锚角石那里看见Tommy

1612
01:32:55.153 --> 01:32:58.862
and having such a huge wash of gratefulness.
被感恩的情绪浸泡着

1613
01:32:59.074 --> 01:33:02.692
[Tommy] Oh! I can’t believe we’re here.
真不敢相信我们都在这儿了

1614
01:33:03.661 --> 01:33:06.323
So good, man.
太好了，老弟

1615
01:33:06.539 --> 01:33:09.155
[Kevin] We’re reunited at our high points now.
我们在彼此的最高绳距处汇合了

1616
01:33:09.375 --> 01:33:11.331
I can’t believe we did it.
无法相信我们都做到了

1617
01:33:11.544 --> 01:33:15.036
Going up from there on out together to the top.
从下往上，一路并肩

1618
01:33:21.971 --> 01:33:24.508
[Tommy] Come on, Jorgeson. Come on.
加油，Kevin Jorgeson，加油

1619
01:33:24.724 --> 01:33:27.557
[Kevin]  He was sitting on five days’ rest while I caught up.
在我追赶的五天里，他坐歇了五天

1620
01:33:27.769 --> 01:33:30.761
Pretty sure he’s going to pull me up the wall today.
今天他肯定要把我拽上岩墙了

1621
01:33:30.980 --> 01:33:34.973
[Tommy] From here on it’s just a matter of grinding it out.
从此以后，就是常规性了

1622
01:33:35.193 --> 01:33:38.060
So we get up and we stay 300 feet from the top.
所以我们起身后，在离开峰顶300英尺的地方停留住

1623
01:33:43.701 --> 01:33:46.238
We wake up this last morning.
最后一个清晨醒来

1624
01:33:46.454 --> 01:33:48.490
The sun comes on the Dawn Wall.
阳光照耀在黎明墙面

1625
01:33:51.501 --> 01:33:52.832
It hits the top of the Wall first,
阳光首先照到岩墙顶端

1626
01:33:53.044 --> 01:33:56.377
and we’re the only thing in Yosemite actually in the sun.
当时我们是优胜美地唯一沐浴在阳光里的人

1627
01:33:56.589 --> 01:33:57.829
[Kevin]So happy.
如此快乐

1628
01:33:59.634 --> 01:34:02.000
[Tommy] This is a good moment right here.
真是好时光

1629
01:34:02.220 --> 01:34:04.211
This is definitely a good moment.
绝对的好时光

1630
01:34:04.430 --> 01:34:06.716
[P Music plays]

1631
01:34:07.892 --> 01:34:09.883
Does it get any better than this?
还能比这更好吗？

1632
01:34:10.103 --> 01:34:12.719
[Tommy] I’m just enjoying my last day
我在享受我最后一天的冲刺

1633
01:34:12.939 --> 01:34:14.770
being up here with my friend.
和我的朋友一起

1634
01:34:14.983 --> 01:34:17.315
I think we should just stay.
我都想就此停下来

1635
01:34:18.611 --> 01:34:19.817
Just cancel the whole thing.
把一切取消

1636
01:34:20.029 --> 01:34:23.442
We’re going to camp here for another day.
再花一天露营

1637
01:34:23.658 --> 01:34:26.195
[kevin] Living on a wall where everything is so simple
住在岩墙上的生活真是简洁

1638
01:34:26.411 --> 01:34:27.526
for 19 days,
19天呐

1639
01:34:27.745 --> 01:34:29.781
we were going to miss that experience.
我们会怀念这段经历的

1640
01:34:29.998 --> 01:34:31.283
[Mark] Good morning to our viewers.
观众朋友早上好

1641
01:34:31.499 --> 01:34:33.990
It’s been an exciting 24 hours here in Yosemite.
刚刚过去的令人激动的24小时，在优胜美地国家公园

1642
01:34:34.210 --> 01:34:35.825
[Ranger] Tommy Caidwell and Kevin Jorgeson
Tommy Caidwell 和 Kevin Jorgeson 两位

1643
01:34:36.045 --> 01:34:37.535
spent 19 days on the Wall.
度过19天的岩墙生活

1644
01:34:37.755 --> 01:34:40.371
There were 15 TV trucks, reporters from all over.
总共有15辆电视台报道卡车，记者们也从四方赶来

1645
01:34:40.592 --> 01:34:41.923
There was a webcam.
还有网络摄像机

1646
01:34:42.135 --> 01:34:43.966
Millions of people were actually watching this live.
数以百万计的人们直接目睹了这实况

1647
01:34:44.179 --> 01:34:45.794
Like a moon landing or something.
几乎类似登月什么了

1648
01:34:48.349 --> 01:34:52.262
A lot of their friends and family had come out.
他们各自的家人和朋友也因此而来

1649
01:34:52.478 --> 01:34:55.436
A number of people hiked up El Cap the back way,
很多人从El Cap的山后背徒步上来

1650
01:34:55.648 --> 01:34:58.640
and you could watch these guys go up the final pitches.
为了亲眼观看这两位完成最后的绳距而上

1651
01:34:58.860 --> 01:35:00.316
And they’re cheering them on.
他们正在欢呼

1652
01:35:00.528 --> 01:35:02.860
[Becca] I love you! Whoo! 我爱你，喔

1653
01:35:04.407 --> 01:35:05.863
It’s gonna be awesome.
真是太棒了

1654
01:35:07.827 --> 01:35:09.909
[Beth] Seeing Tommy do the Dawn Wall,
看到Tommy完成夙愿

1655
01:35:10.121 --> 01:35:12.077
I was super happy for him.
我为他高兴极了

1656
01:35:12.290 --> 01:35:14.656
Just knowing how much was emotionally wrapped up
要知道这包含了多少情感

1657
01:35:14.876 --> 01:35:16.616
in the route for him,
对于他，这一路都是

1658
01:35:17.754 --> 01:35:21.292
I was really proud of him.
我为他自豪

1659
01:35:21.507 --> 01:35:24.749
[Dad] Actually seeing he was going to complete this climb,
亲眼目睹他圆梦攀登

1660
01:35:24.969 --> 01:35:27.585
it was just, wow.
就像，哇塞塞

1661
01:35:30.475 --> 01:35:32.431
[Reporter 1]  After 19 days,
19天后

1662
01:35:32.644 --> 01:35:35.306
Tommy Caidwell pulling himself over the edge of the Dawn Wall.
Tommy Caidwell 在黎明墙的边缘，把自己拽了上去

1663
01:35:40.777 --> 01:35:43.894
Followed minutes later by climbing partner Kevin Jorgeson.
几分钟后，他的搭档Kevin Jorgeson也攀爬了上来

1664
01:35:59.337 --> 01:36:00.873
[Reporter 2] And the crowd cheered
围观人群欢腾起来

1665
01:36:01.089 --> 01:36:04.581
as the two men accomplished a feat many said was impossible.
他们两位完成了众人认为不可能的壮举

1666
01:36:18.398 --> 01:36:20.434
[Branch] There aren’t a lot of moments that choke me up
我轻易不会梗咽

1667
01:36:20.650 --> 01:36:23.312
in sports anymore. I’ve been doing this too long.
在体育项目上，我很久都不会动感情了

1668
01:36:23.528 --> 01:36:26.395
I’ll never forget a scene of them rejoicing.
永远都忘不了他们快乐的那一景

1669
01:36:32.578 --> 01:36:35.661
This is the moment that’s been so many years in the making.
为了完成这一刻，花了多少年

1670
01:36:35.873 --> 01:36:37.659
Now forever enshrined in history.
现在，可以珍藏在历史里了

1671
01:36:37.875 --> 01:36:39.786
[Reporter] Inspiring millions around the world,
鼓舞着全球的人们

1672
01:36:40.003 --> 01:36:41.118
even at the White House,
即使是在白宫

1673
01:36:41.337 --> 01:36:44.204
where President Obama gave a thumbs up.
奥巴马总统都举赞了

1674
01:36:47.260 --> 01:36:48.625
It’s done. It’s done.
完成了，完成了呀

1675
01:36:48.845 --> 01:36:49.925
You are shaking like a leaf.
艾，你都像树叶一样发抖了

1676
01:36:50.138 --> 01:36:51.548
Are you cold or are you emotional?
你是冷呢还是激动过了？

1677
01:36:51.764 --> 01:36:53.470
-I’m emotional. 激动
-OK. 好吧

1678
01:36:53.683 --> 01:36:56.345
[Mom] He’s worked so hard for this.
他为此付出了多少

1679
01:36:56.561 --> 01:37:00.975
[Kevin] That moment he describes as bittersweet.
那一刻，可以描述为苦乐参半

1680
01:37:01.190 --> 01:37:06.480
This whole experience that drove him for so long,
驱动他如此之久的这段经历

1681
01:37:06.696 --> 01:37:08.152
it was over.
就此过去了

1682
01:37:10.199 --> 01:37:13.066
Anything that you’d like to say about El Cap?
有关El Cap，你想说什么吗？

1683
01:37:13.286 --> 01:37:16.699
I’ve totally fallen in love with that piece of rock.
我爱上了那些石头

1684
01:37:16.914 --> 01:37:18.950
It’s been a big centerpiece of my life.
它是我生活的中心

1685
01:37:19.167 --> 01:37:21.658
And I just feel so thankful every day.
每一天我都感恩

1686
01:37:29.886 --> 01:37:32.468
E KEVIN MORBY:
[“I Have Been To The Mountain’9

1687
01:37:38.269 --> 01:37:40.851
[Reporter 1]  Tommy and Kevin join us now on SportsCenter.
Tommy和Kevin在体育中心和我们在一起

1688
01:37:41.064 --> 01:37:43.271
I know Tommy’s lost his voice a little bit.
我知道Tommy嗓子哑了

1689
01:37:43.483 --> 01:37:46.225
[Hoarse voice] It drove me every day for seven years.
七年时间我被它激励

1690
01:37:46.444 --> 01:37:47.433
Sorry. 抱歉

1691
01:37:48.988 --> 01:37:52.947
What did your first real shower in 19 days feel like?
19天才真正冲澡的感觉如何?

1692
01:37:55.119 --> 01:37:58.282
I, like the entire world, was watching you.
我，呃，全球，都在看着你

1693
01:37:58.498 --> 01:38:00.910
And I just thought, why?
我在想，为什么？

1694
01:38:03.252 --> 01:38:06.870
EPAI Throwing out today’s
first pitch, Kevin Jorgeson.
请开出今天的第一棒，Kevin Jorgeson

